-- Clearer policies and Help: Your Privacy Choices, Return Policy, Terms of Service, EULA, Acceptable Use Policy,
-- Disclaimer, Copyright/DMCA, Accessibility Policy, Children's Privacy Notice and Help, made easier to read and
-- true to the November features (In short summaries, content notes, Translate, clips, buddy reads; Help grouped
-- by topic). src/data/legalPages.json has the same. Each page changes only while it still has the built-in
-- wording, so an edit made in the app is never overwritten. Also What's new.

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Accessibility features", "paragraphs": ["You should be able to change colors, contrast levels, and fonts; zoom in up to 200% without loss of information or functionality; navigate the website with just a keyboard, including keyboard shortcuts in the player; listen to the website using a screen reader, with labelled controls; use the read-along transcript with audiobooks; stop moving images with reduced motion; and turn on underlined links.", "The accessibility menu at the top of every page changes text size, theme (dark or light), an easier-to-read font, high contrast, underlined links and reduced motion. Your choices last for the visit.", "Every page works with a keyboard alone, and the player has keyboard shortcuts, listed under its controls. Buttons and links are at least 44 pixels square, focus is always visible, and dialogs keep focus inside them and return it when they close.", "Screen readers hear labelled controls, headings that outline each page, and announcements when something changes, such as a saved setting or a new club post. Pictures that carry meaning, like shared quote cards, have text alternatives; decorative covers are hidden from screen readers and their titles are always written nearby.", "In the reader you can choose the font, size, spacing, margins and theme. Fonts include Lexend and OpenDyslexic, a typeface made for readers with dyslexia, and a reading guide can show a ruler on one line or dim everything but a few lines (line focus); it follows your pointer or a tap, and J and K move it a line. Audiobooks have speed control, a sleep timer, skip lengths you choose, and controls on your lock screen and headphones. The player's read-along transcript follows the narration.", "Newer features follow the same rules. Mood and pace tags are buttons that say whether they're on, content notes and translations are announced when they arrive, a Kids profile's Time for bed screen works with a keyboard and screen reader, and a shared audio clip has a labelled Play button."]}, {"heading": "Compatibility with assistive technology", "paragraphs": ["Our website is designed to be compatible with screen readers and other assistive technologies, using standard HTML and ARIA, in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. We haven't yet completed testing with each screen reader; if yours has trouble, please tell us."]}, {"heading": "Conformance status", "paragraphs": ["Status: partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level AA. Partially conformant means that most of the website conforms, with the exceptions listed under \"What we know isn't perfect yet\".", "We conducted our most recent accessibility evaluation in October 2026. For more information, see \"How we test\"."]}, {"heading": "What we know isn't perfect yet", "paragraphs": ["The read-along transcript for some titles is sample text rather than the exact recording, and is hidden while a real recording plays.", "Book details and covers from Google Books, and the LibriVox recordings, come from other services; we can't always fix problems in their content.", "Books you upload show their text only; images and tables in the original EPUB aren't shown.", "Content notes, translations and other AI-written text can be wrong; they're labelled as written by AI.", "The Google Books preview is Google's own viewer, so we can't change how it works with assistive technology."]}, {"heading": "How we test", "paragraphs": ["Every change is tested with a keyboard, at phone and desktop sizes, and with automated accessibility checks (Lighthouse accessibility scores of 100) before it's released."]}, {"heading": "Feedback and contact information", "paragraphs": ["Please let us know if you experience accessibility barriers using our services or need information in an alternative format. Tell us what you were trying to do, which page it was on, and the browser and assistive technology you use.", "Email: accessibility@literaryworm.com (mark the subject line \"Accessibility\").", "We aim to reply within five working days, and always within 15 business days, and to fix problems that block reading or listening first. We keep a record of accessibility feedback and our replies."]}, {"heading": "Enforcement", "paragraphs": ["If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the enforcement authority in your country: Germany: BFIT-Bund. France: Défenseur des droits. Ireland: National Disability Authority. Spain: OADIS. Italy: AgID. For other EU countries, contact your national consumer protection authority."]}, {"heading": "Preparation of this statement", "paragraphs": ["This statement was prepared on 28 October 2026 and last updated on 1 November 2026. We review it every year, and whenever we make significant changes to the service.", "For questions about accessibility or this statement, email us at accessibility@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$This statement applies to the https://www.literaryworm.com website. LiteraryWorm is committed to ensuring our services are accessible to people with disabilities, so everyone at home can read and listen. We aim to conform with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA.$lw$ then $lw$This statement applies to the https://www.literaryworm.com website. LiteraryWorm is committed to ensuring our services are accessible to people with disabilities, so everyone at home can read and listen. We aim to conform with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at Level AA.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$accessibility$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Accessibility features", "paragraphs": ["You should be able to change colors, contrast levels, and fonts; zoom in up to 200% without loss of information or functionality; navigate the website with just a keyboard, including keyboard shortcuts in the player; listen to the website using a screen reader, with labelled controls; use the read-along transcript with audiobooks; stop moving images with reduced motion; and turn on underlined links.", "The accessibility menu at the top of every page changes text size, theme (dark or light), an easier-to-read font, high contrast, underlined links and reduced motion. Your choices last for the visit.", "Every page works with a keyboard alone, and the player has keyboard shortcuts, listed under its controls. Buttons and links are at least 44 pixels square, focus is always visible, and dialogs keep focus inside them and return it when they close.", "Screen readers hear labelled controls, headings that outline each page, and announcements when something changes, such as a saved setting or a new club post. Pictures that carry meaning, like shared quote cards, have text alternatives; decorative covers are hidden from screen readers and their titles are always written nearby.", "In the reader you can choose the font, size, spacing, margins and theme. Fonts include Lexend and OpenDyslexic, a typeface made for readers with dyslexia, and a reading guide can show a ruler on one line or dim everything but a few lines (line focus); it follows your pointer or a tap, and J and K move it a line. Audiobooks have speed control, a sleep timer, skip lengths you choose, and controls on your lock screen and headphones. The player's read-along transcript follows the narration."]}, {"heading": "Compatibility with assistive technology", "paragraphs": ["Our website is designed to be compatible with screen readers and other assistive technologies, using standard HTML and ARIA, in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. We haven't yet completed testing with each screen reader; if yours has trouble, please tell us."]}, {"heading": "Conformance status", "paragraphs": ["Status: partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level AA. Partially conformant means that most of the website conforms, with the exceptions listed under \"What we know isn't perfect yet\".", "We conducted our most recent accessibility evaluation in October 2026. For more information, see \"How we test\"."]}, {"heading": "What we know isn't perfect yet", "paragraphs": ["The read-along transcript for some titles is sample text rather than the exact recording, and is hidden while a real recording plays.", "Book details and covers from Google Books, and the LibriVox recordings, come from other services; we can't always fix problems in their content.", "Books you upload show their text only; images and tables in the original EPUB aren't shown."]}, {"heading": "How we test", "paragraphs": ["Every change is tested with a keyboard, at phone and desktop sizes, and with automated accessibility checks (Lighthouse accessibility scores of 100) before it's released."]}, {"heading": "Feedback and contact information", "paragraphs": ["Please let us know if you experience accessibility barriers using our services or need information in an alternative format. Tell us what you were trying to do, which page it was on, and the browser and assistive technology you use.", "Email: accessibility@literaryworm.com (mark the subject line \"Accessibility\").", "We aim to reply within five working days, and always within 15 business days, and to fix problems that block reading or listening first. We keep a record of accessibility feedback and our replies."]}, {"heading": "Enforcement", "paragraphs": ["If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the enforcement authority in your country: Germany: BFIT-Bund. France: Défenseur des droits. Ireland: National Disability Authority. Spain: OADIS. Italy: AgID. For other EU countries, contact your national consumer protection authority."]}, {"heading": "Preparation of this statement", "paragraphs": ["This statement was prepared on 28 October 2026 and is reviewed annually or when we make significant service changes.", "For questions about accessibility or this statement, email us at accessibility@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile lives inside your account. Only you, the account holder, can create one, and only after you consent.", "It keeps what it needs to work: a first name or nickname, an avatar and the child's reading. We never ask a child for an email address, full name, photo, location or any way to contact them.", "Its reading is private to your account. It isn't shown to other members, it isn't used for advertising, and it is never sold, rented or licensed.", "You can see it, download it, change its limits or delete it at any time from Account."]}, {"heading": "Your consent comes first", "paragraphs": ["Only the account holder, who must be 18 or older, can create a Kids profile or move a profile to Kids. You do it after reading this notice, and you confirm it with the account password.", "We keep a record of that consent: when it was given, how, and which version of this notice it was for.", "Moving the profile to another age rating, or deleting it, withdraws that consent, and we record that too."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile collects", "paragraphs": ["The profile: its first name or nickname, its avatar, its age rating, and any daily reading limit, weekly reading goal and bedtime you set.", "Its reading: the books in its library, where it is in each book, its bookmarks, highlights and notes, its Up next queue, ratings, the moods and pace it tags books with, favourites and lists, the authors and narrators it follows, and its release reminders.", "Its time: how long it reads and listens each day, in total and for each book (shown on the book's page), the books it finishes, its reading goals and pace, and any reading plan it makes (the day it chose to finish by and where it was when the plan started).", "Its learning: the words it saves from the dictionary and when they're next due for review, its private reading journal, and its chapter quiz scores.", "Its family activity: the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers, and the household challenges it starts or joins, which the other profiles on your account can see.", "Badges are worked out on the device from this reading and are never stored. Books saved for offline reading stay on that device."]}, {"heading": "What we never collect", "paragraphs": ["We don't ask a child for their email address, full name, home address, school, phone number, photo, voice, location or any other way to contact them.", "A Kids profile can't write anything that other members see, so it can't share personal details with them.", "There's no advertising on LiteraryWorm, and we don't use analytics or advertising trackers.", "Kids profiles show only LiteraryWorm's own titles, so Google Books covers and previews, and the third-party cookies Google sets from books.google.com with them, don't load there."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. A grown-up can say yes to a book above that rating when the child asks for it.", "They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, follow other readers, share lists by link, upload or import books, search Google Books, ask the book's AI assistant, translate passages or use Who's who.", "They can't make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "AI features", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile can read AI-written book summaries and content notes, hear a recap of earlier chapters (Previously…) and take chapter quizzes. These are written by Claude, made by Anthropic.", "We send Anthropic only the book's details or its own text and which chapter it's about, never the child's name, answers, scores or anything else about them. The summaries, content notes, recaps and quizzes are kept and shared with every reader of that book, so they say nothing about who asked."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["You do: Account → Family shows each Kids profile's last 7 days, its weekly goal, its book requests and its quiz scores.", "If you turn on the weekly Kids reading report, we email last week's reading to your account's email address. Mailgun sends it for us. It's off until you turn it on.", "Our hosting providers, Supabase and Vercel, store and serve it only to run LiteraryWorm for you.", "Our support team can see how many profiles an account has, but not a profile's name, library, reading, notes or journal."]}, {"heading": "How long we keep it", "paragraphs": ["We keep a Kids profile's information for as long as the profile exists.", "Deleting the profile, or your whole account, deletes everything it collected from our database straight away. Copies in our providers' backups are removed when those backups expire."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see the profile's activity, download a copy of your data, change its daily limit, weekly goal, bedtime and age rating, and answer its book requests.", "You can add a PIN to the other profiles so a child can't open them.", "You can stop us collecting anything more at any time by deleting the profile, which deletes everything it collected. Moving it to another age rating also ends the Kids protections, but keeps its reading under its new rating."]}, {"heading": "Keeping it safe", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile's information is stored with access rules, so only your account can read it. Our support team can't see a profile's name, library or reading.", "You can protect the account with two-step sign-in or a passkey, and lock other profiles with a PIN, which we keep only as a one-way hash."]}, {"heading": "Changes to this notice", "paragraphs": ["We keep the version of this notice you agreed to with each Kids profile. If we change what a Kids profile collects, we'll update this notice and say so on What's new."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have a question about your child's information, or think a child is using LiteraryWorm without a parent's consent, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com. We'll answer, and we'll delete information collected without consent.", "The Privacy Policy explains how we handle everyone's information, including your rights where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$For parents and guardians: what a Kids profile collects, why, who can see it, what we never collect, and how you stay in control. A Kids profile exists only with your consent, and you can see, download or delete everything it keeps.$lw$ then $lw$For parents and guardians: what a Kids profile collects, why, who can see it, what we never collect, and how you stay in control. A Kids profile exists only with your consent, and you can see, download or delete everything it keeps.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$childrens-privacy$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile lives inside your account. Only you, the account holder, can create one, and only after you consent.", "It keeps what it needs to work: a first name or nickname, an avatar and the child's reading. We never ask a child for an email address, full name, photo, location or any way to contact them.", "Its reading is private to your account. It isn't shown to other members, it isn't used for advertising, and it is never sold, rented or licensed.", "You can see it, download it, change its limits or delete it at any time from Account."]}, {"heading": "Your consent comes first", "paragraphs": ["Only the account holder, who must be 18 or older, can create a Kids profile or move a profile to Kids. You do it after reading this notice, and you confirm it with the account password.", "We keep a record of that consent: when it was given, how, and which version of this notice it was for.", "Moving the profile to another age rating, or deleting it, withdraws that consent, and we record that too."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile collects", "paragraphs": ["The profile: its first name or nickname, its avatar, its age rating, and any daily reading limit, weekly reading goal and bedtime you set.", "Its reading: the books in its library, where it is in each book, its bookmarks, highlights and notes, its Up next queue, ratings, the moods and pace it tags books with, favourites and lists, the authors and narrators it follows, and its release reminders.", "Its time: how long it reads and listens each day, in total and for each book (shown on the book's page), the books it finishes, its reading goals and pace, and any reading plan it makes (the day it chose to finish by and where it was when the plan started).", "Its learning: the words it saves from the dictionary and when they're next due for review, its private reading journal, and its chapter quiz scores.", "Its family activity: the books it asks a grown-up for and your answers, and the household challenges it starts or joins, which the other profiles on your account can see.", "Badges are worked out on the device from this reading and are never stored. Books saved for offline reading stay on that device."]}, {"heading": "What we never collect", "paragraphs": ["We don't ask a child for their email address, full name, home address, school, phone number, photo, voice, location or any other way to contact them.", "A Kids profile can't write anything that other members see, so it can't share personal details with them.", "There's no advertising on LiteraryWorm, and we don't use analytics or advertising trackers.", "Kids profiles show only LiteraryWorm's own titles, so Google Books covers and previews, and the third-party cookies Google sets from books.google.com with them, don't load there."]}, {"heading": "What a Kids profile can't do", "paragraphs": ["Kids profiles see only books rated for children. A grown-up can say yes to a book above that rating when the child asks for it.", "They can't write public reading logs, join or start book clubs, follow other readers, share lists by link, upload or import books, search Google Books, ask the book's AI assistant, translate passages or use Who's who.", "They can't make purchases or change account settings. A grown-up's password is needed to open Account or to allow extra time past a daily limit."]}, {"heading": "AI features", "paragraphs": ["A Kids profile can read AI-written book summaries and content notes, hear a recap of earlier chapters (Previously…) and take chapter quizzes. These are written by Claude, made by Anthropic.", "We send Anthropic only the book's details or its own text and which chapter it's about, never the child's name, answers, scores or anything else about them. The summaries, content notes, recaps and quizzes are kept and shared with every reader of that book, so they say nothing about who asked."]}, {"heading": "Who sees it", "paragraphs": ["You do: Account → Family shows each Kids profile's last 7 days, its weekly goal, its book requests and its quiz scores.", "If you turn on the weekly Kids reading report, we email last week's reading to your account's email address. Mailgun sends it for us. It's off until you turn it on.", "Our hosting providers, Supabase and Vercel, store and serve it only to run LiteraryWorm for you.", "Our support team can see how many profiles an account has, but not a profile's name, library, reading, notes or journal."]}, {"heading": "How long we keep it", "paragraphs": ["We keep a Kids profile's information for as long as the profile exists.", "Deleting the profile, or your whole account, deletes everything it collected from our database straight away. Copies in our providers' backups are removed when those backups expire."]}, {"heading": "Your choices as a parent", "paragraphs": ["From Account you can see the profile's activity, download a copy of your data, change its daily limit, weekly goal, bedtime and age rating, and answer its book requests.", "You can add a PIN to the other profiles so a child can't open them.", "You can stop us collecting anything more at any time by deleting the profile, which deletes everything it collected. Moving it to another age rating also ends the Kids protections, but keeps its reading under its new rating."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have a question about your child's information, or think a child is using LiteraryWorm without a parent's consent, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com. We'll answer, and we'll delete information collected without consent.", "The Privacy Policy explains how we handle everyone's information, including your rights where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for advertising. There's nothing to opt out of there, and Global Privacy Control is honoured.", "You decide which emails and notifications you get, what your browser keeps, what other members see, and whether your data stays. You can change each of these in Account at any time."]}, {"heading": "Selling and sharing", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.", "If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a request to opt out. Nothing changes, because we already don't do either."]}, {"heading": "Emails", "paragraphs": ["In Account → Preferences, turn each kind of email on or off: books you set Remind me on coming out, new books from authors you follow, club meeting reminders and changes, a daily email of new club posts, the weekly Kids reading report, the monthly What's new, and marketing emails. Several are off until you turn them on.", "Each of these emails has an unsubscribe link that works in one click. Emails about your account, such as confirming your address or resetting your password, always arrive."]}, {"heading": "Notifications on your devices", "paragraphs": ["Notifications on this device, in Account → Preferences, are off until you turn them on, and are set for each device. Choose which ones you get: books coming out, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, the evening streak nudge and answers to Kids book requests.", "Logging out on a device turns them off there. Each book club also has its own alerts switch on its page."]}, {"heading": "Cookies and browser storage", "paragraphs": ["We set no advertising or analytics cookies. Our backend's host, Cloudflare, sets one cookie to keep out bots, and Google sets third-party cookies from books.google.com when Google Books covers and previews load, because we use the Google Books API.", "Change your cookie choice with Consent Preferences at the bottom of every page, and block third-party cookies in your browser to stop Google's. The Cookie Policy lists everything your browser keeps and how to clear it."]}, {"heading": "What other members see", "paragraphs": ["Your library, progress, notes, highlights, journal, moods and saved words are private to your household. Reading logs you publish show on the book's page with your display name.", "Your reader page, which gathers your public reading logs, is off until you turn it on, and turning it off removes its followers. In each book club, Show my place is off until you turn it on."]}, {"heading": "Your data", "paragraphs": ["In Account you can download a copy of your data, correct your display name, and delete profiles or your whole account.", "Reading logs, club posts, shared highlights, saved words, journal entries and uploads can each be deleted whenever you like. The Privacy Policy explains what we keep and for how long."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["Email usprivacy@literaryworm.com with any question about your privacy choices, or to make a request under the law where you live."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$LiteraryWorm doesn't sell or share personal information for advertising and uses no non-essential cookies (see the Cookie Policy), so there's nothing to opt out of there. Global Privacy Control is honoured. Here are the choices you do have.$lw$ then $lw$The choices you have about your information on LiteraryWorm. We don't sell it or share it for advertising, and you control your emails, notifications, cookies and data from Account.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$privacy-choices$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Selling and sharing", "paragraphs": ["We don't sell, rent or license your personal information, and we don't share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a request to opt out, and nothing changes because we already don't do either."]}, {"heading": "Cookies and browser storage", "paragraphs": ["We set no cookies of our own and no advertising or analytics cookies. The Cookie Policy lists the strictly necessary things your browser keeps, such as your sign-in session, and how to clear them."]}, {"heading": "Emails and notifications", "paragraphs": ["Turn emails about new releases and offers on or off in Account → Preferences. Service emails, like password resets, always arrive. Book club alerts can be turned off for each club on its page, and browser notifications only appear if you allow them. Notifications about books you set Remind me on are turned on and off for each device in Account → Preferences, and logging out on a device turns them off there."]}, {"heading": "Your data", "paragraphs": ["In Account you can download a copy of your data, correct your display name, and delete profiles or your whole account. Reading logs, club posts, highlights, saved words and uploads can each be deleted whenever you like, and your reader page can be turned off. The Privacy Policy explains what we keep and for how long."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Agreement to our legal terms", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms constitute a legally binding agreement made between you, whether personally or on behalf of an entity (\"you\"), and LiteraryWorm, concerning your access to and use of the Services. You agree that by accessing the Services, you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by all of these Legal Terms. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE WITH ALL OF THESE LEGAL TERMS, THEN YOU ARE EXPRESSLY PROHIBITED FROM USING THE SERVICES AND YOU MUST DISCONTINUE USE IMMEDIATELY.", "Supplemental terms and conditions or documents that may be posted on the Services from time to time, such as our End User License Agreement (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/eula), are hereby expressly incorporated herein by reference. We may change these Legal Terms from time to time. We'll tell you before changing them in ways that matter, and we'll update the \"Last updated\" date.", "You will be subject to, and will be deemed to have accepted, the changes in any revised Legal Terms by your continued use of the Services after the date such revised Legal Terms are posted.", "Account holders must be at least 18 years old. People under 18 may use the Services only through a profile, such as a Kids profile, that a parent or guardian adds to their own account and is responsible for.", "We recommend that you print a copy of these Legal Terms for your records."]}, {"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["This summary helps you find your way around these Legal Terms. It doesn't replace them.", "You must be 18 or older to have an account. Kids and Teen profiles are added by the account holder, who is responsible for them.", "Memberships renew monthly or yearly until you cancel. Cancel at least 48 hours before your billing date to stop the next charge, and know that payments are final (section 30 and the Return Policy).", "You may read and listen for yourself and your household, but not copy, share or sell the books (section 31).", "You own what you write, and you give us a licence only to show it where you posted it (section 33). Upload only books you have the right to read (section 34).", "Follow the Acceptable Use Policy. We may suspend or close accounts that break these Legal Terms (section 16).", "AI-written content is labelled and may be wrong, and the Services are provided as they are (sections 21 and 22). Disputes go to informal negotiation first (section 19)."]}, {"heading": "1. Our services", "paragraphs": ["The information provided when using the Services is not intended for distribution to or use by any person or entity in any jurisdiction or country where such distribution or use would be contrary to law or regulation or which would subject us to any registration requirement within such jurisdiction or country.", "Accordingly, those persons who choose to access the Services from other locations do so on their own initiative and are solely responsible for compliance with local laws, if and to the extent local laws are applicable.", "The Services are not tailored to comply with industry-specific regulations (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), Federal Information Security Management Act (FISMA), etc.), so if your interactions would be subjected to such laws, you may not use the Services. You may not use the Services in a way that would violate the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act (GLBA)."]}, {"heading": "2. Intellectual property rights", "paragraphs": ["Our intellectual property. We are the owner or the licensee of all intellectual property rights in our Services, including all source code, databases, functionality, software, website designs, audio, video, text, photographs, and graphics in the Services (collectively, the \"Content\"), as well as the trademarks, service marks, and logos contained therein (the \"Marks\"). Section 32 explains which books are in the public domain and who owns the rest.", "Our Content and Marks are protected by copyright and trademark laws (and various other intellectual property rights and unfair competition laws) and treaties in the United States and around the world.", "The Content and Marks are provided in or through the Services \"AS IS\" for your personal, non-commercial use only.", "Your use of our Services. Subject to your compliance with these Legal Terms, including the \"Prohibited activities\" section below, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access the Services, solely for your personal, non-commercial use. What you may do with the books is set out in section 31.", "Except as set out in this section or elsewhere in our Legal Terms, no part of the Services and no Content or Marks may be copied, reproduced, aggregated, republished, uploaded, posted, publicly displayed, encoded, translated, transmitted, distributed, sold, licensed, or otherwise exploited for any commercial purpose whatsoever, without our express prior written permission.", "If you wish to make any use of the Services, Content, or Marks other than as set out in this section or elsewhere in our Legal Terms, please address your request to: support@literaryworm.com.", "If we ever grant you the permission to post, reproduce, or publicly display any part of our Services or Content, you must identify us as the owners or licensors of the Services, Content, or Marks and ensure that any copyright or proprietary notice appears or is visible on posting, reproducing, or displaying our Content.", "We reserve all rights not expressly granted to you in and to the Services, Content, and Marks. Being able to see source code we publish doesn't give you a license to use it.", "Any breach of these Intellectual Property Rights will constitute a material breach of our Legal Terms and your right to use our Services will terminate immediately.", "Your submissions. By directly sending us any question, comment, suggestion, idea, feedback, or other information about the Services (\"Submissions\"), you agree to assign to us all intellectual property rights in such Submission. You agree that we shall own this Submission and be entitled to its unrestricted use and dissemination for any lawful purpose, commercial or otherwise, without acknowledgment or compensation to you.", "Your contributions. What you post in the Services (reading logs, club posts, ratings, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights) are \"Contributions\", covered by sections 9, 10 and 33. You own them, and the license you give us is the limited one in section 33. Contributions you make public may be seen by anyone, including through links you share outside the Services.", "You are responsible for what you post or upload. By sending us Submissions and/or posting Contributions, you:", "confirm that you have read and agree with our \"Prohibited activities\" and will not post, send, publish, upload, or transmit through the Services any Submission nor post any Contribution that is illegal, harassing, hateful, harmful, defamatory, obscene, bullying, abusive, discriminatory, threatening to any person or group, sexually explicit, false, inaccurate, deceitful, or misleading;", "warrant that any such Submission and/or Contributions are original to you or that you have the necessary rights and licenses to submit them and full authority to grant us the rights in these Legal Terms;", "and warrant and represent that your Submissions and/or Contributions do not constitute confidential information.", "You are solely responsible for your Submissions and/or Contributions and you expressly agree to reimburse us for any and all losses that we may suffer because of your breach of (a) this section, (b) any third party's intellectual property rights, or (c) applicable law.", "We may remove your Contributions. Although we have no obligation to monitor any Contributions, we shall have the right to remove any Contributions at any time without notice if in our reasonable opinion we consider such Contributions harmful or in breach of these Legal Terms. If we remove any such Contributions, we may also suspend or disable your account and report you to the authorities.", "Copyright infringement. We respect the intellectual property rights of others. If you believe that any material available on or through the Services infringes upon any copyright you own or control, please refer to section 15 and our Copyright/DMCA page."]}, {"heading": "3. User representations", "paragraphs": ["By using the Services, you represent and warrant that:", "(1) all registration information you submit will be true, accurate, current, and complete;", "(2) you will maintain the accuracy of such information and promptly update such registration information as necessary;", "(3) you have the legal capacity and you agree to comply with these Legal Terms;", "(4) if you hold an account, you are at least 18 and not a minor in the jurisdiction in which you reside;", "(5) you will not access the Services through automated or non-human means, whether through a bot, script or otherwise;", "(6) you will not use the Services for any illegal or unauthorized purpose;", "and (7) your use of the Services will not violate any applicable law or regulation.", "If you provide any information that is untrue, inaccurate, not current, or incomplete, we have the right to suspend or terminate your account and refuse any and all current or future use of the Services (or any portion thereof)."]}, {"heading": "4. User registration", "paragraphs": ["You need to register to use most of the Services. You agree to keep your password confidential and will be responsible for all use of your account and password. We reserve the right to remove, reclaim, or change a display name or profile name you select if we determine, in our sole discretion, that it is inappropriate, obscene, or otherwise objectionable."]}, {"heading": "5. Purchases and payment", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is a live service: when you choose a plan, you're billed monthly or yearly (as you choose) through Stripe until you cancel. Add a payment method in Account → Plan and billing to continue your membership.", "We accept the following forms of payment: Visa, Mastercard, American Express and Discover.", "You agree to provide current, complete, and accurate purchase and account information for all purchases made via the Services. You further agree to promptly update account and payment information, including email address, payment method, and payment card expiration date, so that we can complete your transactions and contact you as needed. Sales tax will be added to the price of purchases as deemed required by us. We may change prices at any time. All payments shall be in US dollars.", "You agree to pay all charges at the prices then in effect for your purchases, and you authorize us to charge your chosen payment provider for any such amounts upon placing your order. We reserve the right to correct any errors or mistakes in pricing, even if we have already requested or received payment.", "We reserve the right to refuse any order placed through the Services. We may, in our sole discretion, limit or cancel quantities purchased per person, per household, or per order. These restrictions may include orders placed by or under the same customer account or the same payment method. We reserve the right to limit or prohibit orders that, in our sole judgment, appear to be placed by dealers, resellers, or distributors."]}, {"heading": "6. Subscriptions", "paragraphs": ["Billing and renewal. Your subscription will continue and automatically renew each month on your billing day (or, if you pay yearly, each year on the date your year started) unless canceled. You consent to our charging your payment method on a recurring basis without requiring your prior approval for each recurring charge, until such time as you cancel. You can change your billing day to any day from the 1st to the 28th in Account.", "Cancellation and pausing. You can pause, resume or cancel your subscription at any time from Account. A pause stops billing until you resume. To stop the next charge, cancel at least 48 hours before your next billing date: your cancellation then takes effect at the end of the current paid term.", "If you cancel less than 48 hours before your billing date, that charge still goes through and your cancellation takes effect at the end of the term it pays for. No refunds are given for any part of a term. If you have any questions or are unsatisfied with our Services, please email us at support@literaryworm.com.", "Fee changes. We may, from time to time, make changes to the subscription fee and will communicate any price changes to you in accordance with applicable law."]}, {"heading": "7. Software", "paragraphs": ["Our End User License Agreement (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/eula) governs your use of the LiteraryWorm app, in the browser or installed on a device. Any other software we provide in connection with our Services is licensed to you on a non-exclusive, revocable, personal, and non-transferable basis, solely in connection with our Services and in accordance with these Legal Terms.", "Any software and any related documentation is provided \"AS IS\" without warranty of any kind, either express or implied, including, without limitation, the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. You accept any and all risk arising out of use or performance of any software. You may not reproduce or redistribute any software except in accordance with the EULA or these Legal Terms."]}, {"heading": "8. Prohibited activities", "paragraphs": ["You may not access or use the Services for any purpose other than that for which we make the Services available. The Services may not be used in connection with any commercial endeavors except those that are specifically endorsed or approved by us.", "As a user of the Services, you agree not to:", "1. Systematically retrieve data or other content from the Services to create or compile, directly or indirectly, a collection, compilation, database, or directory without written permission from us.", "2. Trick, defraud, or mislead us and other users, especially in any attempt to learn sensitive account information such as user passwords or profile PINs.", "3. Circumvent, disable, or otherwise interfere with security-related features of the Services, including features that prevent or restrict the use or copying of any Content or enforce limitations on the use of the Services and/or the Content contained therein, such as daily reading limits and age ratings.", "4. Disparage, tarnish, or otherwise harm, in our opinion, us and/or the Services.", "5. Use any information obtained from the Services in order to harass, abuse, or harm another person.", "6. Make improper use of our support services or submit false reports of abuse or misconduct.", "7. Use the Services in a manner inconsistent with any applicable laws or regulations.", "8. Engage in unauthorized framing of or linking to the Services.", "9. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) viruses, Trojan horses, or other material, including excessive use of capital letters and spamming (continuous posting of repetitive text), that interferes with any party's uninterrupted use and enjoyment of the Services or modifies, impairs, disrupts, alters, or interferes with the use, features, functions, operation, or maintenance of the Services.", "10. Engage in any automated use of the system, such as using scripts to send comments or messages, or using any data mining, robots, or similar data gathering and extraction tools.", "11. Delete the copyright or other proprietary rights notice from any Content.", "12. Attempt to impersonate another user or person or use the display name of another user.", "13. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) any material that acts as a passive or active information collection or transmission mechanism, including without limitation, clear graphics interchange formats (\"gifs\"), 1×1 pixels, web bugs, cookies, or other similar devices (sometimes referred to as \"spyware\" or \"passive collection mechanisms\" or \"pcms\").", "14. Interfere with, disrupt, or create an undue burden on the Services or the networks or services connected to the Services, including by trying to get around the limits on AI summaries, content notes, Ask the book, Translate, Who's who, Previously… recaps and chapter quizzes and Previously… recaps.", "15. Harass, annoy, intimidate, or threaten any of our employees or agents engaged in providing any portion of the Services to you.", "16. Attempt to bypass any measures of the Services designed to prevent or restrict access to the Services, or any portion of the Services.", "17. Copy or adapt the Services' software, including but not limited to HTML, JavaScript, or other code.", "18. Except as permitted by applicable law, decipher, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer any of the software comprising or in any way making up a part of the Services.", "19. Except as may be the result of standard search engine or Internet browser usage, or the Services' own Read offline feature, use, launch, develop, or distribute any automated system, including without limitation, any spider, robot, cheat utility, scraper, or offline reader that accesses the Services, or use or launch any unauthorized script or other software.", "20. Use a buying agent or purchasing agent to make purchases on the Services.", "21. Make any unauthorized use of the Services, including collecting display names and/or email addresses of users by electronic or other means for the purpose of sending unsolicited email, or creating user accounts by automated means or under false pretenses.", "22. Use the Services as part of any effort to compete with us or otherwise use the Services and/or the Content for any revenue-generating endeavor or commercial enterprise.", "23. Sell or otherwise transfer your account or a profile.", "24. Use the Services to advertise or offer to sell goods and services."]}, {"heading": "9. User generated contributions", "paragraphs": ["The Services invite you to post Contributions: reading logs (shown on a book's public page with your display name), book club posts (seen by the club's members), highlights you share with a club (seen by its members), ratings, lists you choose to share by link, and private notes and highlights. Contributions you make public may be viewable by other users of the Services and by anyone you share a link with. When you create or make available any Contributions, you thereby represent and warrant that:", "1. The creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party.", "2. You are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Services, and other users of the Services to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and these Legal Terms.", "3. You have the written consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and these Legal Terms.", "4. Your Contributions are not false, inaccurate, or misleading.", "5. Your Contributions are not unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation.", "6. Your Contributions are not obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, or otherwise objectionable (as determined by us).", "7. Your Contributions do not ridicule, mock, disparage, intimidate, or abuse anyone.", "8. Your Contributions are not used to harass or threaten (in the legal sense of those terms) any other person and to promote violence against a specific person or class of people.", "9. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law, regulation, or rule.", "10. Your Contributions do not violate the privacy or publicity rights of any third party.", "11. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law concerning child sexual abuse material, or otherwise intended to protect the health or well-being of minors.", "12. Your Contributions do not include any offensive comments that are connected to race, national origin, gender, sexual preference, or physical handicap.", "13. Your Contributions do not otherwise violate, or link to material that violates, any provision of these Legal Terms, or any applicable law or regulation.", "Any use of the Services in violation of the foregoing violates these Legal Terms and may result in, among other things, termination or suspension of your rights to use the Services."]}, {"heading": "10. Contribution license", "paragraphs": ["We do not assert any ownership over your Contributions. You retain full ownership of all of your Contributions and any intellectual property rights or other proprietary rights associated with your Contributions. The only license you give us is the one in section 33: to store, copy and display them where and to whom you posted them, so we can run the features you use.", "We are not liable for any statements or representations in your Contributions provided by you in any area on the Services. You are solely responsible for your Contributions to the Services and you expressly agree to exonerate us from any and all responsibility and to refrain from any legal action against us regarding your Contributions.", "We have the right, in our sole and absolute discretion, to remove or hide any Contributions at any time and for any reason, without notice. We have no obligation to monitor your Contributions."]}, {"heading": "11. Guidelines for reviews", "paragraphs": ["You can rate books and write about them in reading logs. When you do, you must comply with the following criteria:", "(1) you should have firsthand experience with the book you're reviewing;", "(2) your reviews should not contain offensive profanity, or abusive, racist, offensive, or hateful language;", "(3) your reviews should not contain discriminatory references based on religion, race, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, or disability;", "(4) your reviews should not contain references to illegal activity;", "(5) you should not be affiliated with competitors if posting negative reviews;", "(6) you should not make any conclusions as to the legality of conduct;", "(7) you may not post any false or misleading statements;", "and (8) you may not organize a campaign encouraging others to post reviews, whether positive or negative.", "We may remove reviews in our sole discretion. We have absolutely no obligation to screen reviews or to delete reviews, even if anyone considers reviews objectionable or inaccurate. Reviews are not endorsed by us, and do not necessarily represent our opinions or the views of any of our affiliates or partners. We do not assume liability for any review or for any claims, liabilities, or losses resulting from any review. Reviews are Contributions, so you keep them, and the license you give us is the one in section 33."]}, {"heading": "12. Third-party websites and content", "paragraphs": ["The Services contain (or you may be sent via the Site) links to other websites (\"Third-Party Websites\"), such as Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg, as well as articles, photographs, text, graphics, pictures, designs, music, sound, video, information, applications, software, and other content or items belonging to or originating from third parties (\"Third-Party Content\"), such as book details and covers from Google Books and recordings from LibriVox.", "Such Third-Party Websites and Third-Party Content are not investigated, monitored, or checked for accuracy, appropriateness, or completeness by us, and we are not responsible for any Third-Party Websites accessed through the Services or any Third-Party Content posted on, available through, or installed from the Services, including the content, accuracy, offensiveness, opinions, reliability, privacy practices, or other policies of or contained in the Third-Party Websites or the Third-Party Content.", "Inclusion of, linking to, or permitting the use or installation of any Third-Party Websites or any Third-Party Content does not imply approval or endorsement thereof by us. If you decide to leave the Services and access the Third-Party Websites or to use or install any Third-Party Content, you do so at your own risk, and you should be aware these Legal Terms no longer govern.", "You should review the applicable terms and policies, including privacy and data gathering practices, of any website to which you navigate from the Services or relating to any applications you use or install from the Services.", "Any purchases you make through Third-Party Websites will be through other websites and from other companies, and we take no responsibility whatsoever in relation to such purchases which are exclusively between you and the applicable third party.", "You agree and acknowledge that we do not endorse the products or services offered on Third-Party Websites and you shall hold us blameless from any harm caused by your purchase of such products or services. Additionally, you shall hold us blameless from any losses sustained by you or harm caused to you relating to or resulting in any way from any Third-Party Content or any contact with Third-Party Websites."]}, {"heading": "13. Services management", "paragraphs": ["We reserve the right, but not the obligation, to:", "(1) monitor the Services for violations of these Legal Terms;", "(2) take appropriate legal action against anyone who, in our sole discretion, violates the law or these Legal Terms, including without limitation, reporting such user to law enforcement authorities;", "(3) in our sole discretion and without limitation, refuse, restrict access to, limit the availability of, or disable (to the extent technologically feasible) any of your Contributions or any portion thereof;", "(4) in our sole discretion and without limitation, notice, or liability, to remove from the Services or otherwise disable all files and content that are excessive in size or are in any way burdensome to our systems;", "and (5) otherwise manage the Services in a manner designed to protect our rights and property and to facilitate the proper functioning of the Services."]}, {"heading": "14. Privacy policy", "paragraphs": ["We care about data privacy and security. Please review our Privacy Policy: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/privacy. By using the Services, you agree to be bound by our Privacy Policy, which is incorporated into these Legal Terms. Please be advised the Services are hosted in the United States.", "If you access the Services from any other region of the world with laws or other requirements governing personal data collection, use, or disclosure that differ from applicable laws in the United States, then through your continued use of the Services, you are transferring your data to the United States, and you expressly consent to have your data transferred to and processed in the United States."]}, {"heading": "15. Copyright infringements", "paragraphs": ["We respect the intellectual property rights of others. If you believe that any material available on or through the Services infringes upon any copyright you own or control, please follow the steps on our Copyright/DMCA page (a \"Notification\"). We will tell the member who posted the material that it was removed.", "Please be advised that pursuant to applicable law you may be held liable for damages if you make material misrepresentations in a Notification. Thus, if you are not sure that material located on or linked to by the Services infringes your copyright, you should consider first contacting an attorney."]}, {"heading": "16. Term and termination", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms shall remain in full force and effect while you use the Services. You can end them at any time by deleting your account from Account.", "WITHOUT LIMITING ANY OTHER PROVISION OF THESE LEGAL TERMS, WE RESERVE THE RIGHT TO, IN OUR SOLE DISCRETION AND WITHOUT NOTICE OR LIABILITY, DENY ACCESS TO AND USE OF THE SERVICES (INCLUDING BLOCKING CERTAIN IP ADDRESSES), TO ANY PERSON FOR ANY REASON OR FOR NO REASON, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION FOR BREACH OF ANY REPRESENTATION, WARRANTY, OR COVENANT CONTAINED IN THESE LEGAL TERMS OR OF ANY APPLICABLE LAW OR REGULATION.", "WE MAY TERMINATE YOUR USE OR PARTICIPATION IN THE SERVICES OR DELETE YOUR ACCOUNT AND ANY CONTENT OR INFORMATION THAT YOU POSTED AT ANY TIME, WITHOUT WARNING, IN OUR SOLE DISCRETION.", "If we terminate or suspend your account for any reason, you are prohibited from registering and creating a new account under your name, a fake or borrowed name, or the name of any third party, even if you may be acting on behalf of the third party. In addition to terminating or suspending your account, we reserve the right to take appropriate legal action, including without limitation pursuing civil, criminal, and injunctive redress."]}, {"heading": "17. Modifications and interruptions", "paragraphs": ["We reserve the right to change, modify, or remove the contents of the Services at any time or for any reason at our sole discretion without notice. However, we have no obligation to update any information on our Services. We will not be liable to you or any third party for any modification, price change, suspension, or discontinuance of the Services.", "We cannot guarantee the Services will be available at all times. We may experience hardware, software, or other problems or need to perform maintenance related to the Services, resulting in interruptions, delays, or errors. Our Status page shows whether the Services are working.", "We reserve the right to change, revise, update, suspend, discontinue, or otherwise modify the Services at any time or for any reason without notice to you. You agree that we have no liability whatsoever for any loss, damage, or inconvenience caused by your inability to access or use the Services during any downtime or discontinuance of the Services.", "Nothing in these Legal Terms will be construed to obligate us to maintain and support the Services or to supply any corrections, updates, or releases in connection therewith."]}, {"heading": "18. Governing law", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms and your use of the Services are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Illinois applicable to agreements made and to be entirely performed within the State of Illinois, without regard to its conflict of law principles."]}, {"heading": "19. Dispute resolution", "paragraphs": ["Informal negotiations. To expedite resolution and control the cost of any dispute, controversy, or claim related to these Legal Terms (each a \"Dispute\" and collectively, the \"Disputes\") brought by either you or us (individually, a \"Party\" and collectively, the \"Parties\"), the Parties agree to first attempt to negotiate any Dispute (except those Disputes expressly provided below) informally for at least thirty (30) days before initiating arbitration. Such informal negotiations commence upon written notice from one Party to the other Party.", "Binding arbitration. If the Parties are unable to resolve a Dispute through informal negotiations, the Dispute (except those Disputes expressly excluded below) will be finally and exclusively resolved by binding arbitration. YOU UNDERSTAND THAT WITHOUT THIS PROVISION, YOU WOULD HAVE THE RIGHT TO SUE IN COURT AND HAVE A JURY TRIAL.", "The arbitration shall be commenced and conducted under the Commercial Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association (\"AAA\") and, where appropriate, the AAA's Supplementary Procedures for Consumer Related Disputes (\"AAA Consumer Rules\"), both of which are available at the American Arbitration Association (AAA) website.", "Your arbitration fees and your share of arbitrator compensation shall be governed by the AAA Consumer Rules and, where appropriate, limited by the AAA Consumer Rules. The arbitration may be conducted in person, through the submission of documents, by phone, or online. The arbitrator will make a decision in writing, but need not provide a statement of reasons unless requested by either Party.", "The arbitrator must follow applicable law, and any award may be challenged if the arbitrator fails to do so. Except where otherwise required by the applicable AAA rules or applicable law, the arbitration will take place in Cook County, Illinois.", "Except as otherwise provided herein, the Parties may litigate in court to compel arbitration, stay proceedings pending arbitration, or to confirm, modify, vacate, or enter judgment on the award entered by the arbitrator.", "If for any reason, a Dispute proceeds in court rather than arbitration, the Dispute shall be commenced or prosecuted in the state and federal courts located in Cook County, Illinois, and the Parties hereby consent to, and waive all defenses of lack of personal jurisdiction, and forum non conveniens with respect to venue and jurisdiction in such state and federal courts.", "Application of the United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods and the Uniform Computer Information Transaction Act (UCITA) are excluded from these Legal Terms.", "In no event shall any Dispute brought by either Party related in any way to the Services be commenced more than one (1) year after the cause of action arose.", "If this provision is found to be illegal or unenforceable, then neither Party will elect to arbitrate any Dispute falling within that portion of this provision found to be illegal or unenforceable and such Dispute shall be decided by a court of competent jurisdiction within the courts listed for jurisdiction above, and the Parties agree to submit to the personal jurisdiction of that court.", "Restrictions. The Parties agree that any arbitration shall be limited to the Dispute between the Parties individually.", "To the full extent permitted by law, (a) no arbitration shall be joined with any other proceeding; (b) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be arbitrated on a class-action basis or to utilize class action procedures; and (c) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be brought in a purported representative capacity on behalf of the general public or any other persons.", "Exceptions to informal negotiations and arbitration. The Parties agree that the following Disputes are not subject to the above provisions concerning informal negotiations and binding arbitration: (a) any Disputes seeking to enforce or protect, or concerning the validity of, any of the intellectual property rights of a Party; (b) any Dispute related to, or arising from, allegations of theft, piracy, invasion of privacy, or unauthorized use; and (c) any claim for injunctive relief.", "If this provision is found to be illegal or unenforceable, then neither Party will elect to arbitrate any Dispute falling within that portion of this provision found to be illegal or unenforceable and such Dispute shall be decided by a court of competent jurisdiction within the courts listed for jurisdiction above, and the Parties agree to submit to the personal jurisdiction of that court."]}, {"heading": "20. Corrections", "paragraphs": ["There may be information on the Services that contains typographical errors, inaccuracies, or omissions, including descriptions, pricing, availability, and various other information. We reserve the right to correct any errors, inaccuracies, or omissions and to change or update the information on the Services at any time, without prior notice."]}, {"heading": "21. Disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED ON AN AS-IS AND AS-AVAILABLE BASIS. YOU AGREE THAT YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES WILL BE AT YOUR SOLE RISK. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE DISCLAIM ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, IN CONNECTION WITH THE SERVICES AND YOUR USE THEREOF, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.", "WE MAKE NO WARRANTIES OR REPRESENTATIONS ABOUT THE ACCURACY OR COMPLETENESS OF THE SERVICES' CONTENT (INCLUDING BOOK DETAILS FROM GOOGLE BOOKS AND SUMMARIES, CONTENT NOTES, TRANSLATIONS AND ANSWERS WRITTEN BY AI) OR THE CONTENT OF ANY WEBSITES OR MOBILE APPLICATIONS LINKED TO THE SERVICES AND WE WILL ASSUME NO LIABILITY OR RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY:", "(1) ERRORS, MISTAKES, OR INACCURACIES OF CONTENT AND MATERIALS,", "(2) PERSONAL INJURY OR PROPERTY DAMAGE, OF ANY NATURE WHATSOEVER, RESULTING FROM YOUR ACCESS TO AND USE OF THE SERVICES,", "(3) ANY UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO OR USE OF OUR SECURE SERVERS AND/OR ANY AND ALL PERSONAL INFORMATION STORED THEREIN,", "(4) ANY INTERRUPTION OR CESSATION OF TRANSMISSION TO OR FROM THE SERVICES,", "(5) ANY BUGS, VIRUSES, TROJAN HORSES, OR THE LIKE WHICH MAY BE TRANSMITTED TO OR THROUGH THE SERVICES BY ANY THIRD PARTY,", "AND/OR (6) ANY ERRORS OR OMISSIONS IN ANY CONTENT AND MATERIALS OR FOR ANY LOSS OR DAMAGE OF ANY KIND INCURRED AS A RESULT OF THE USE OF ANY CONTENT POSTED, TRANSMITTED, OR OTHERWISE MADE AVAILABLE VIA THE SERVICES.", "WE DO NOT WARRANT, ENDORSE, GUARANTEE, OR ASSUME RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY PRODUCT OR SERVICE OFFERED BY A THIRD PARTY THROUGH THE SERVICES OR ANY HYPERLINKED WEBSITE, AND WE WILL NOT BE A PARTY TO OR IN ANY WAY BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MONITORING ANY TRANSACTION BETWEEN YOU AND ANY THIRD-PARTY PROVIDERS OF PRODUCTS OR SERVICES.", "AS WITH THE PURCHASE OF A PRODUCT OR SERVICE THROUGH ANY MEDIUM OR IN ANY ENVIRONMENT, YOU SHOULD USE YOUR BEST JUDGMENT AND EXERCISE CAUTION WHERE APPROPRIATE."]}, {"heading": "22. Limitations of liability", "paragraphs": ["IN NO EVENT WILL WE OR OUR DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AGENTS BE LIABLE TO YOU OR ANY THIRD PARTY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFIT, LOST REVENUE, LOSS OF DATA, OR OTHER DAMAGES ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.", "NOTWITHSTANDING ANYTHING TO THE CONTRARY CONTAINED HEREIN, OUR LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY CAUSE WHATSOEVER AND REGARDLESS OF THE FORM OF THE ACTION, WILL AT ALL TIMES BE LIMITED TO THE AMOUNT PAID, IF ANY, BY YOU TO US DURING THE SIX (6) MONTH PERIOD PRIOR TO ANY CAUSE OF ACTION ARISING.", "CERTAIN US STATE LAWS AND INTERNATIONAL LAWS DO NOT ALLOW LIMITATIONS ON IMPLIED WARRANTIES OR THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF CERTAIN DAMAGES. IF THESE LAWS APPLY TO YOU, SOME OR ALL OF THE ABOVE DISCLAIMERS OR LIMITATIONS MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU, AND YOU MAY HAVE ADDITIONAL RIGHTS."]}, {"heading": "23. Indemnification", "paragraphs": ["You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold us harmless, including our subsidiaries, affiliates, and all of our respective officers, agents, partners, and employees, from and against any loss, damage, liability, claim, or demand, including reasonable attorneys' fees and expenses, made by any third party due to or arising out of:", "(1) your Contributions;", "(2) use of the Services;", "(3) breach of these Legal Terms;", "(4) any breach of your representations and warranties set forth in these Legal Terms;", "(5) your violation of the rights of a third party, including but not limited to intellectual property rights;", "or (6) any overt harmful act toward any other user of the Services with whom you connected via the Services.", "Notwithstanding the foregoing, we reserve the right, at your expense, to assume the exclusive defense and control of any matter for which you are required to indemnify us, and you agree to cooperate, at your expense, with our defense of such claims. We will use reasonable efforts to notify you of any such claim, action, or proceeding which is subject to this indemnification upon becoming aware of it."]}, {"heading": "24. User data", "paragraphs": ["We will maintain certain data that you transmit to the Services for the purpose of managing the performance of the Services, as well as data relating to your use of the Services, as our Privacy Policy describes. You can download a copy of your data at any time from Account (Download my data).", "To the extent permitted by law, you are responsible for keeping your own copy of anything you can't afford to lose, and you agree that we shall have no liability to you for any loss or corruption of any such data."]}, {"heading": "25. Electronic communications, transactions, and signatures", "paragraphs": ["Visiting the Services, sending us emails, and completing online forms constitute electronic communications. You consent to receive electronic communications, and you agree that all agreements, notices, disclosures, and other communications we provide to you electronically, via email and on the Services, satisfy any legal requirement that such communication be in writing.", "YOU HEREBY AGREE TO THE USE OF ELECTRONIC SIGNATURES, CONTRACTS, ORDERS, AND OTHER RECORDS, AND TO ELECTRONIC DELIVERY OF NOTICES, POLICIES, AND RECORDS OF TRANSACTIONS INITIATED OR COMPLETED BY US OR VIA THE SERVICES.", "You hereby waive any rights or requirements under any statutes, regulations, rules, ordinances, or other laws in any jurisdiction which require an original signature or delivery or retention of non-electronic records, or to payments or the granting of credits by any means other than electronic means."]}, {"heading": "26. SMS text messaging", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm doesn't send text messages (SMS) and doesn't ask for your phone number. If we ever start a text messaging program, we'll add its terms here, including how to opt out, before it begins."]}, {"heading": "27. California users and residents", "paragraphs": ["If any complaint with us is not satisfactorily resolved, you can contact the Complaint Assistance Unit of the Division of Consumer Services of the California Department of Consumer Affairs in writing at 1625 North Market Blvd., Suite N 112, Sacramento, California 95834 or by telephone at (800) 952-5210 or (916) 445-1254."]}, {"heading": "28. Miscellaneous", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms and any policies or operating rules posted by us on the Services or in respect to the Services constitute the entire agreement and understanding between you and us. Our failure to exercise or enforce any right or provision of these Legal Terms shall not operate as a waiver of such right or provision. These Legal Terms operate to the fullest extent permissible by law.", "We may assign any or all of our rights and obligations to others at any time. We shall not be responsible or liable for any loss, damage, delay, or failure to act caused by any cause beyond our reasonable control.", "If any provision or part of a provision of these Legal Terms is determined to be unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that provision or part of the provision is deemed severable from these Legal Terms and does not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions.", "There is no joint venture, partnership, employment or agency relationship created between you and us as a result of these Legal Terms or use of the Services. You agree that these Legal Terms will not be construed against us by virtue of having drafted them.", "You hereby waive any and all defenses you may have based on the electronic form of these Legal Terms and the lack of signing by the parties hereto to execute these Legal Terms."]}, {"heading": "29. Your account", "paragraphs": ["Account holders must be 18 or older. You may add profiles for people in your household, including Kids profiles with your consent, and you're responsible for how they're used.", "Keep your password private. You can change it, and delete your account, from Account at any time."]}, {"heading": "30. Membership", "paragraphs": ["Plans renew automatically each month on your billing day until you cancel, which you can do online at any time; reading continues until the end of the period you've paid for. Cancel at least 48 hours before your billing date to stop the next charge; cancelling later means one more monthly charge, and then the membership ends. No refunds.", "You can change your billing day (the 1st to the 28th), and pause and resume, from Account. Yearly plans cost ten times the monthly price, start the day you pay and renew on that date each year until you cancel; we remind you in the app 30 days before. The same 48 hours' notice applies, so cancelling later means one more yearly charge.", "Moving from monthly to yearly starts the year at once, with the unused part of the month taken off its price; moving a yearly plan to a bigger plan charges the difference for the rest of the year straight away, and to a smaller one takes effect at renewal with no credit. Yearly plans can't be paused or change their billing day.", "You can choose monthly billing at any time, and it starts on your renewal date, with nothing charged or refunded before then.", "This is not a demo app anymore: your LiteraryWorm account is a live account. You'll be billed monthly, or yearly if you choose, until you cancel. Add a payment method in Account → Plan and billing to continue your membership. On monthly billing you can change your billing day to any day from the 1st to the 28th, and start, pause or cancel billing at any time in Account; a yearly plan can be cancelled at any time, but not paused.", "Plan limits. Each plan includes the audiobook listening, profiles and offline devices shown on the Plans page: Basic, 5 hours a month, 1 profile and 1 device; Standard, 30 hours, 3 profiles and 10 devices; Premium, unlimited listening, 12 profiles and 24 devices. Listening is counted for the whole household on every device.", "When a month's hours are used up, audiobooks pause until the 1st of the next month; reading carries on, and you can change plan at any time. To move to a plan with fewer profiles or offline devices, first set aside or remove the profiles and free the devices it has no room for.", "A household that already has more profiles than its plan now allows, because the plan changed, keeps them in use but can't add more until it fits. A profile set aside keeps its shelf, history and settings, doesn't count towards the plan, and comes back when there's room. While a yearly membership waits to move to a smaller plan at renewal, it has that plan's room already.", "Each device that saves books with Read offline holds one of the plan's places: free one in Account → Plan and billing to use another device, and the freed device's offline books are removed the next time it opens LiteraryWorm.", "Staff memberships. People with a LiteraryWorm staff role (admin, editor, developer, billing, customer service, blog or sales) have a complimentary Premium membership for as long as they hold a role. It's never billed and can't be paused or cancelled; it ends when their last staff role is removed, and they can then choose a plan like any member."]}, {"heading": "31. Your licence to read and listen", "paragraphs": ["While your membership is active, we give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to read and listen to the books in LiteraryWorm for your own and your household's non-commercial use, in the app.", "You may not copy, sell, share, broadcast or publicly perform the books, remove or get around any protection on them, or use them to train AI models. Books saved for offline reading stay in the app on your device.", "This licence doesn't apply to public-domain works themselves, which anyone may use freely; it covers our app, our edition and our service."]}, {"heading": "32. Who owns the books and the app", "paragraphs": ["Public-domain titles: the texts come from Project Gutenberg and the recordings from LibriVox, whose volunteers release their recordings into the public domain. These works are in the public domain in the United States; they may not be everywhere, so check your country's rules before using them outside LiteraryWorm.", "Other LiteraryWorm titles show sample pages, not the published books. Book details and covers from Google Books belong to their publishers and rights holders and are shown under Google's terms.", "Summaries, content notes, Ask the book answers, translations, Who's who, Previously… recaps and chapter quizzes are written by AI (Claude) and labelled so. They may be wrong; they're provided for your own reading and may not be republished as LiteraryWorm's.", "The LiteraryWorm name, logo, design and software belong to LiteraryWorm. Using the service doesn't give you any rights in them beyond these Terms."]}, {"heading": "33. What you post, and the license you give us", "paragraphs": ["You own what you write: reading logs, club posts, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights.", "So we can run the features you use, you give LiteraryWorm a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to store, copy and display what you post, only where and to whom you posted it (logs on the book's public page with your display name, club posts to the club, shared lists to anyone with the link). The licence ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies already made by others, such as someone else's screenshot.", "Notes, highlights, saved words and private lists are never shown to anyone else."]}, {"heading": "34. Books you upload", "paragraphs": ["Upload only books you have the right to read in this way, such as DRM-free books you've bought or works in the public domain. Don't upload books you don't have rights to, and don't remove DRM to upload them.", "Your uploads stay private to the profile that added them. We store their text only to show it to you, claim no rights in them, and delete them when you do or when you delete the profile or account.", "You can start a book club around a book you uploaded. Its members see only the title and author; each of them reads their own copy, which they must also have the right to read, and nobody's upload is shared with anyone else."]}, {"heading": "35. Rules, changes and ending", "paragraphs": ["Don't post anything unlawful, hateful, harassing or infringing, impersonate others, spam clubs, or try to break or overload the service. We may remove content that breaks these rules and suspend accounts that keep doing so, including repeat copyright infringers (see Copyright/DMCA).", "LiteraryWorm is provided as is. We'll tell you before changing these Terms in ways that matter, and you can cancel or delete your account at any time."]}, {"heading": "36. Contact us", "paragraphs": ["In order to resolve a complaint regarding the Services or to receive further information regarding use of the Services, please contact us at: LiteraryWorm, support@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$We are LiteraryWorm ("Company," "we," "us," "our"). We operate the website https://www.literaryworm.com (the "Site"), as well as any other related products and services that refer or link to these legal terms (the "Legal Terms") (collectively, the "Services"). These Legal Terms cover who can have an account, how membership works, what you may do with the books, who owns what, and the license you give us for what you post. You can contact us by email at support@literaryworm.com.$lw$ then $lw$We are LiteraryWorm ("Company," "we," "us," "our"). We operate the website https://www.literaryworm.com (the "Site"), as well as any other related products and services that refer or link to these legal terms (the "Legal Terms") (collectively, the "Services"). These Legal Terms cover who can have an account, how membership works, what you may do with the books, who owns what, and the license you give us for what you post. You can contact us by email at support@literaryworm.com.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$terms$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Agreement to our legal terms", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms constitute a legally binding agreement made between you, whether personally or on behalf of an entity (\"you\"), and LiteraryWorm, concerning your access to and use of the Services. You agree that by accessing the Services, you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by all of these Legal Terms. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE WITH ALL OF THESE LEGAL TERMS, THEN YOU ARE EXPRESSLY PROHIBITED FROM USING THE SERVICES AND YOU MUST DISCONTINUE USE IMMEDIATELY.", "Supplemental terms and conditions or documents that may be posted on the Services from time to time, such as our End User License Agreement (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/eula), are hereby expressly incorporated herein by reference. We may change these Legal Terms from time to time. We'll tell you before changing them in ways that matter, and we'll update the \"Last updated\" date.", "You will be subject to, and will be deemed to have accepted, the changes in any revised Legal Terms by your continued use of the Services after the date such revised Legal Terms are posted.", "Account holders must be at least 18 years old. People under 18 may use the Services only through a profile, such as a Kids profile, that a parent or guardian adds to their own account and is responsible for.", "We recommend that you print a copy of these Legal Terms for your records."]}, {"heading": "1. Our services", "paragraphs": ["The information provided when using the Services is not intended for distribution to or use by any person or entity in any jurisdiction or country where such distribution or use would be contrary to law or regulation or which would subject us to any registration requirement within such jurisdiction or country.", "Accordingly, those persons who choose to access the Services from other locations do so on their own initiative and are solely responsible for compliance with local laws, if and to the extent local laws are applicable.", "The Services are not tailored to comply with industry-specific regulations (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), Federal Information Security Management Act (FISMA), etc.), so if your interactions would be subjected to such laws, you may not use the Services. You may not use the Services in a way that would violate the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act (GLBA)."]}, {"heading": "2. Intellectual property rights", "paragraphs": ["Our intellectual property. We are the owner or the licensee of all intellectual property rights in our Services, including all source code, databases, functionality, software, website designs, audio, video, text, photographs, and graphics in the Services (collectively, the \"Content\"), as well as the trademarks, service marks, and logos contained therein (the \"Marks\"). Section 32 explains which books are in the public domain and who owns the rest.", "Our Content and Marks are protected by copyright and trademark laws (and various other intellectual property rights and unfair competition laws) and treaties in the United States and around the world.", "The Content and Marks are provided in or through the Services \"AS IS\" for your personal, non-commercial use only.", "Your use of our Services. Subject to your compliance with these Legal Terms, including the \"Prohibited activities\" section below, we grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access the Services, solely for your personal, non-commercial use. What you may do with the books is set out in section 31.", "Except as set out in this section or elsewhere in our Legal Terms, no part of the Services and no Content or Marks may be copied, reproduced, aggregated, republished, uploaded, posted, publicly displayed, encoded, translated, transmitted, distributed, sold, licensed, or otherwise exploited for any commercial purpose whatsoever, without our express prior written permission.", "If you wish to make any use of the Services, Content, or Marks other than as set out in this section or elsewhere in our Legal Terms, please address your request to: support@literaryworm.com.", "If we ever grant you the permission to post, reproduce, or publicly display any part of our Services or Content, you must identify us as the owners or licensors of the Services, Content, or Marks and ensure that any copyright or proprietary notice appears or is visible on posting, reproducing, or displaying our Content.", "We reserve all rights not expressly granted to you in and to the Services, Content, and Marks. Being able to see source code we publish doesn't give you a license to use it.", "Any breach of these Intellectual Property Rights will constitute a material breach of our Legal Terms and your right to use our Services will terminate immediately.", "Your submissions. By directly sending us any question, comment, suggestion, idea, feedback, or other information about the Services (\"Submissions\"), you agree to assign to us all intellectual property rights in such Submission. You agree that we shall own this Submission and be entitled to its unrestricted use and dissemination for any lawful purpose, commercial or otherwise, without acknowledgment or compensation to you.", "Your contributions. What you post in the Services (reading logs, club posts, ratings, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights) are \"Contributions\", covered by sections 9, 10 and 33. You own them, and the license you give us is the limited one in section 33. Contributions you make public may be seen by anyone, including through links you share outside the Services.", "You are responsible for what you post or upload. By sending us Submissions and/or posting Contributions, you:", "confirm that you have read and agree with our \"Prohibited activities\" and will not post, send, publish, upload, or transmit through the Services any Submission nor post any Contribution that is illegal, harassing, hateful, harmful, defamatory, obscene, bullying, abusive, discriminatory, threatening to any person or group, sexually explicit, false, inaccurate, deceitful, or misleading;", "warrant that any such Submission and/or Contributions are original to you or that you have the necessary rights and licenses to submit them and full authority to grant us the rights in these Legal Terms;", "and warrant and represent that your Submissions and/or Contributions do not constitute confidential information.", "You are solely responsible for your Submissions and/or Contributions and you expressly agree to reimburse us for any and all losses that we may suffer because of your breach of (a) this section, (b) any third party's intellectual property rights, or (c) applicable law.", "We may remove your Contributions. Although we have no obligation to monitor any Contributions, we shall have the right to remove any Contributions at any time without notice if in our reasonable opinion we consider such Contributions harmful or in breach of these Legal Terms. If we remove any such Contributions, we may also suspend or disable your account and report you to the authorities.", "Copyright infringement. We respect the intellectual property rights of others. If you believe that any material available on or through the Services infringes upon any copyright you own or control, please refer to section 15 and our Copyright/DMCA page."]}, {"heading": "3. User representations", "paragraphs": ["By using the Services, you represent and warrant that:", "(1) all registration information you submit will be true, accurate, current, and complete;", "(2) you will maintain the accuracy of such information and promptly update such registration information as necessary;", "(3) you have the legal capacity and you agree to comply with these Legal Terms;", "(4) if you hold an account, you are at least 18 and not a minor in the jurisdiction in which you reside;", "(5) you will not access the Services through automated or non-human means, whether through a bot, script or otherwise;", "(6) you will not use the Services for any illegal or unauthorized purpose;", "and (7) your use of the Services will not violate any applicable law or regulation.", "If you provide any information that is untrue, inaccurate, not current, or incomplete, we have the right to suspend or terminate your account and refuse any and all current or future use of the Services (or any portion thereof)."]}, {"heading": "4. User registration", "paragraphs": ["You need to register to use most of the Services. You agree to keep your password confidential and will be responsible for all use of your account and password. We reserve the right to remove, reclaim, or change a display name or profile name you select if we determine, in our sole discretion, that it is inappropriate, obscene, or otherwise objectionable."]}, {"heading": "5. Purchases and payment", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is a live service: when you choose a plan, you're billed monthly or yearly (as you choose) through Stripe until you cancel. Add a payment method in Account → Plan and billing to continue your membership.", "We accept the following forms of payment: Visa, Mastercard, American Express and Discover.", "You agree to provide current, complete, and accurate purchase and account information for all purchases made via the Services. You further agree to promptly update account and payment information, including email address, payment method, and payment card expiration date, so that we can complete your transactions and contact you as needed. Sales tax will be added to the price of purchases as deemed required by us. We may change prices at any time. All payments shall be in US dollars.", "You agree to pay all charges at the prices then in effect for your purchases, and you authorize us to charge your chosen payment provider for any such amounts upon placing your order. We reserve the right to correct any errors or mistakes in pricing, even if we have already requested or received payment.", "We reserve the right to refuse any order placed through the Services. We may, in our sole discretion, limit or cancel quantities purchased per person, per household, or per order. These restrictions may include orders placed by or under the same customer account or the same payment method. We reserve the right to limit or prohibit orders that, in our sole judgment, appear to be placed by dealers, resellers, or distributors."]}, {"heading": "6. Subscriptions", "paragraphs": ["Billing and renewal. Your subscription will continue and automatically renew each month on your billing day (or, if you pay yearly, each year on the date your year started) unless canceled. You consent to our charging your payment method on a recurring basis without requiring your prior approval for each recurring charge, until such time as you cancel. You can change your billing day to any day from the 1st to the 28th in Account.", "Cancellation and pausing. You can pause, resume or cancel your subscription at any time from Account. A pause stops billing until you resume. To stop the next charge, cancel at least 48 hours before your next billing date: your cancellation then takes effect at the end of the current paid term.", "If you cancel less than 48 hours before your billing date, that charge still goes through and your cancellation takes effect at the end of the term it pays for. No refunds are given for any part of a term. If you have any questions or are unsatisfied with our Services, please email us at support@literaryworm.com.", "Fee changes. We may, from time to time, make changes to the subscription fee and will communicate any price changes to you in accordance with applicable law."]}, {"heading": "7. Software", "paragraphs": ["Our End User License Agreement (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/eula) governs your use of the LiteraryWorm app, in the browser or installed on a device. Any other software we provide in connection with our Services is licensed to you on a non-exclusive, revocable, personal, and non-transferable basis, solely in connection with our Services and in accordance with these Legal Terms.", "Any software and any related documentation is provided \"AS IS\" without warranty of any kind, either express or implied, including, without limitation, the implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. You accept any and all risk arising out of use or performance of any software. You may not reproduce or redistribute any software except in accordance with the EULA or these Legal Terms."]}, {"heading": "8. Prohibited activities", "paragraphs": ["You may not access or use the Services for any purpose other than that for which we make the Services available. The Services may not be used in connection with any commercial endeavors except those that are specifically endorsed or approved by us.", "As a user of the Services, you agree not to:", "1. Systematically retrieve data or other content from the Services to create or compile, directly or indirectly, a collection, compilation, database, or directory without written permission from us.", "2. Trick, defraud, or mislead us and other users, especially in any attempt to learn sensitive account information such as user passwords or profile PINs.", "3. Circumvent, disable, or otherwise interfere with security-related features of the Services, including features that prevent or restrict the use or copying of any Content or enforce limitations on the use of the Services and/or the Content contained therein, such as daily reading limits and age ratings.", "4. Disparage, tarnish, or otherwise harm, in our opinion, us and/or the Services.", "5. Use any information obtained from the Services in order to harass, abuse, or harm another person.", "6. Make improper use of our support services or submit false reports of abuse or misconduct.", "7. Use the Services in a manner inconsistent with any applicable laws or regulations.", "8. Engage in unauthorized framing of or linking to the Services.", "9. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) viruses, Trojan horses, or other material, including excessive use of capital letters and spamming (continuous posting of repetitive text), that interferes with any party's uninterrupted use and enjoyment of the Services or modifies, impairs, disrupts, alters, or interferes with the use, features, functions, operation, or maintenance of the Services.", "10. Engage in any automated use of the system, such as using scripts to send comments or messages, or using any data mining, robots, or similar data gathering and extraction tools.", "11. Delete the copyright or other proprietary rights notice from any Content.", "12. Attempt to impersonate another user or person or use the display name of another user.", "13. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) any material that acts as a passive or active information collection or transmission mechanism, including without limitation, clear graphics interchange formats (\"gifs\"), 1×1 pixels, web bugs, cookies, or other similar devices (sometimes referred to as \"spyware\" or \"passive collection mechanisms\" or \"pcms\").", "14. Interfere with, disrupt, or create an undue burden on the Services or the networks or services connected to the Services, including by trying to get around the limits on AI summaries, Ask the book, Who's who and chapter quizzes and Previously… recaps.", "15. Harass, annoy, intimidate, or threaten any of our employees or agents engaged in providing any portion of the Services to you.", "16. Attempt to bypass any measures of the Services designed to prevent or restrict access to the Services, or any portion of the Services.", "17. Copy or adapt the Services' software, including but not limited to HTML, JavaScript, or other code.", "18. Except as permitted by applicable law, decipher, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer any of the software comprising or in any way making up a part of the Services.", "19. Except as may be the result of standard search engine or Internet browser usage, or the Services' own Read offline feature, use, launch, develop, or distribute any automated system, including without limitation, any spider, robot, cheat utility, scraper, or offline reader that accesses the Services, or use or launch any unauthorized script or other software.", "20. Use a buying agent or purchasing agent to make purchases on the Services.", "21. Make any unauthorized use of the Services, including collecting display names and/or email addresses of users by electronic or other means for the purpose of sending unsolicited email, or creating user accounts by automated means or under false pretenses.", "22. Use the Services as part of any effort to compete with us or otherwise use the Services and/or the Content for any revenue-generating endeavor or commercial enterprise.", "23. Sell or otherwise transfer your account or a profile.", "24. Use the Services to advertise or offer to sell goods and services."]}, {"heading": "9. User generated contributions", "paragraphs": ["The Services invite you to post Contributions: reading logs (shown on a book's public page with your display name), book club posts (seen by the club's members), highlights you share with a club (seen by its members), ratings, lists you choose to share by link, and private notes and highlights. Contributions you make public may be viewable by other users of the Services and by anyone you share a link with. When you create or make available any Contributions, you thereby represent and warrant that:", "1. The creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party.", "2. You are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Services, and other users of the Services to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and these Legal Terms.", "3. You have the written consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and these Legal Terms.", "4. Your Contributions are not false, inaccurate, or misleading.", "5. Your Contributions are not unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation.", "6. Your Contributions are not obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, or otherwise objectionable (as determined by us).", "7. Your Contributions do not ridicule, mock, disparage, intimidate, or abuse anyone.", "8. Your Contributions are not used to harass or threaten (in the legal sense of those terms) any other person and to promote violence against a specific person or class of people.", "9. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law, regulation, or rule.", "10. Your Contributions do not violate the privacy or publicity rights of any third party.", "11. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law concerning child sexual abuse material, or otherwise intended to protect the health or well-being of minors.", "12. Your Contributions do not include any offensive comments that are connected to race, national origin, gender, sexual preference, or physical handicap.", "13. Your Contributions do not otherwise violate, or link to material that violates, any provision of these Legal Terms, or any applicable law or regulation.", "Any use of the Services in violation of the foregoing violates these Legal Terms and may result in, among other things, termination or suspension of your rights to use the Services."]}, {"heading": "10. Contribution license", "paragraphs": ["We do not assert any ownership over your Contributions. You retain full ownership of all of your Contributions and any intellectual property rights or other proprietary rights associated with your Contributions. The only license you give us is the one in section 33: to store, copy and display them where and to whom you posted them, so we can run the features you use.", "We are not liable for any statements or representations in your Contributions provided by you in any area on the Services. You are solely responsible for your Contributions to the Services and you expressly agree to exonerate us from any and all responsibility and to refrain from any legal action against us regarding your Contributions.", "We have the right, in our sole and absolute discretion, to remove or hide any Contributions at any time and for any reason, without notice. We have no obligation to monitor your Contributions."]}, {"heading": "11. Guidelines for reviews", "paragraphs": ["You can rate books and write about them in reading logs. When you do, you must comply with the following criteria:", "(1) you should have firsthand experience with the book you're reviewing;", "(2) your reviews should not contain offensive profanity, or abusive, racist, offensive, or hateful language;", "(3) your reviews should not contain discriminatory references based on religion, race, gender, national origin, age, marital status, sexual orientation, or disability;", "(4) your reviews should not contain references to illegal activity;", "(5) you should not be affiliated with competitors if posting negative reviews;", "(6) you should not make any conclusions as to the legality of conduct;", "(7) you may not post any false or misleading statements;", "and (8) you may not organize a campaign encouraging others to post reviews, whether positive or negative.", "We may remove reviews in our sole discretion. We have absolutely no obligation to screen reviews or to delete reviews, even if anyone considers reviews objectionable or inaccurate. Reviews are not endorsed by us, and do not necessarily represent our opinions or the views of any of our affiliates or partners. We do not assume liability for any review or for any claims, liabilities, or losses resulting from any review. Reviews are Contributions, so you keep them, and the license you give us is the one in section 33."]}, {"heading": "12. Third-party websites and content", "paragraphs": ["The Services contain (or you may be sent via the Site) links to other websites (\"Third-Party Websites\"), such as Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg, as well as articles, photographs, text, graphics, pictures, designs, music, sound, video, information, applications, software, and other content or items belonging to or originating from third parties (\"Third-Party Content\"), such as book details and covers from Google Books and recordings from LibriVox.", "Such Third-Party Websites and Third-Party Content are not investigated, monitored, or checked for accuracy, appropriateness, or completeness by us, and we are not responsible for any Third-Party Websites accessed through the Services or any Third-Party Content posted on, available through, or installed from the Services, including the content, accuracy, offensiveness, opinions, reliability, privacy practices, or other policies of or contained in the Third-Party Websites or the Third-Party Content.", "Inclusion of, linking to, or permitting the use or installation of any Third-Party Websites or any Third-Party Content does not imply approval or endorsement thereof by us. If you decide to leave the Services and access the Third-Party Websites or to use or install any Third-Party Content, you do so at your own risk, and you should be aware these Legal Terms no longer govern.", "You should review the applicable terms and policies, including privacy and data gathering practices, of any website to which you navigate from the Services or relating to any applications you use or install from the Services.", "Any purchases you make through Third-Party Websites will be through other websites and from other companies, and we take no responsibility whatsoever in relation to such purchases which are exclusively between you and the applicable third party.", "You agree and acknowledge that we do not endorse the products or services offered on Third-Party Websites and you shall hold us blameless from any harm caused by your purchase of such products or services. Additionally, you shall hold us blameless from any losses sustained by you or harm caused to you relating to or resulting in any way from any Third-Party Content or any contact with Third-Party Websites."]}, {"heading": "13. Services management", "paragraphs": ["We reserve the right, but not the obligation, to:", "(1) monitor the Services for violations of these Legal Terms;", "(2) take appropriate legal action against anyone who, in our sole discretion, violates the law or these Legal Terms, including without limitation, reporting such user to law enforcement authorities;", "(3) in our sole discretion and without limitation, refuse, restrict access to, limit the availability of, or disable (to the extent technologically feasible) any of your Contributions or any portion thereof;", "(4) in our sole discretion and without limitation, notice, or liability, to remove from the Services or otherwise disable all files and content that are excessive in size or are in any way burdensome to our systems;", "and (5) otherwise manage the Services in a manner designed to protect our rights and property and to facilitate the proper functioning of the Services."]}, {"heading": "14. Privacy policy", "paragraphs": ["We care about data privacy and security. Please review our Privacy Policy: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/privacy. By using the Services, you agree to be bound by our Privacy Policy, which is incorporated into these Legal Terms. Please be advised the Services are hosted in the United States.", "If you access the Services from any other region of the world with laws or other requirements governing personal data collection, use, or disclosure that differ from applicable laws in the United States, then through your continued use of the Services, you are transferring your data to the United States, and you expressly consent to have your data transferred to and processed in the United States."]}, {"heading": "15. Copyright infringements", "paragraphs": ["We respect the intellectual property rights of others. If you believe that any material available on or through the Services infringes upon any copyright you own or control, please follow the steps on our Copyright/DMCA page (a \"Notification\"). We will tell the member who posted the material that it was removed.", "Please be advised that pursuant to applicable law you may be held liable for damages if you make material misrepresentations in a Notification. Thus, if you are not sure that material located on or linked to by the Services infringes your copyright, you should consider first contacting an attorney."]}, {"heading": "16. Term and termination", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms shall remain in full force and effect while you use the Services. You can end them at any time by deleting your account from Account.", "WITHOUT LIMITING ANY OTHER PROVISION OF THESE LEGAL TERMS, WE RESERVE THE RIGHT TO, IN OUR SOLE DISCRETION AND WITHOUT NOTICE OR LIABILITY, DENY ACCESS TO AND USE OF THE SERVICES (INCLUDING BLOCKING CERTAIN IP ADDRESSES), TO ANY PERSON FOR ANY REASON OR FOR NO REASON, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION FOR BREACH OF ANY REPRESENTATION, WARRANTY, OR COVENANT CONTAINED IN THESE LEGAL TERMS OR OF ANY APPLICABLE LAW OR REGULATION.", "WE MAY TERMINATE YOUR USE OR PARTICIPATION IN THE SERVICES OR DELETE YOUR ACCOUNT AND ANY CONTENT OR INFORMATION THAT YOU POSTED AT ANY TIME, WITHOUT WARNING, IN OUR SOLE DISCRETION.", "If we terminate or suspend your account for any reason, you are prohibited from registering and creating a new account under your name, a fake or borrowed name, or the name of any third party, even if you may be acting on behalf of the third party. In addition to terminating or suspending your account, we reserve the right to take appropriate legal action, including without limitation pursuing civil, criminal, and injunctive redress."]}, {"heading": "17. Modifications and interruptions", "paragraphs": ["We reserve the right to change, modify, or remove the contents of the Services at any time or for any reason at our sole discretion without notice. However, we have no obligation to update any information on our Services. We will not be liable to you or any third party for any modification, price change, suspension, or discontinuance of the Services.", "We cannot guarantee the Services will be available at all times. We may experience hardware, software, or other problems or need to perform maintenance related to the Services, resulting in interruptions, delays, or errors. Our Status page shows whether the Services are working.", "We reserve the right to change, revise, update, suspend, discontinue, or otherwise modify the Services at any time or for any reason without notice to you. You agree that we have no liability whatsoever for any loss, damage, or inconvenience caused by your inability to access or use the Services during any downtime or discontinuance of the Services.", "Nothing in these Legal Terms will be construed to obligate us to maintain and support the Services or to supply any corrections, updates, or releases in connection therewith."]}, {"heading": "18. Governing law", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms and your use of the Services are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Illinois applicable to agreements made and to be entirely performed within the State of Illinois, without regard to its conflict of law principles."]}, {"heading": "19. Dispute resolution", "paragraphs": ["Informal negotiations. To expedite resolution and control the cost of any dispute, controversy, or claim related to these Legal Terms (each a \"Dispute\" and collectively, the \"Disputes\") brought by either you or us (individually, a \"Party\" and collectively, the \"Parties\"), the Parties agree to first attempt to negotiate any Dispute (except those Disputes expressly provided below) informally for at least thirty (30) days before initiating arbitration. Such informal negotiations commence upon written notice from one Party to the other Party.", "Binding arbitration. If the Parties are unable to resolve a Dispute through informal negotiations, the Dispute (except those Disputes expressly excluded below) will be finally and exclusively resolved by binding arbitration. YOU UNDERSTAND THAT WITHOUT THIS PROVISION, YOU WOULD HAVE THE RIGHT TO SUE IN COURT AND HAVE A JURY TRIAL.", "The arbitration shall be commenced and conducted under the Commercial Arbitration Rules of the American Arbitration Association (\"AAA\") and, where appropriate, the AAA's Supplementary Procedures for Consumer Related Disputes (\"AAA Consumer Rules\"), both of which are available at the American Arbitration Association (AAA) website.", "Your arbitration fees and your share of arbitrator compensation shall be governed by the AAA Consumer Rules and, where appropriate, limited by the AAA Consumer Rules. The arbitration may be conducted in person, through the submission of documents, by phone, or online. The arbitrator will make a decision in writing, but need not provide a statement of reasons unless requested by either Party.", "The arbitrator must follow applicable law, and any award may be challenged if the arbitrator fails to do so. Except where otherwise required by the applicable AAA rules or applicable law, the arbitration will take place in Cook County, Illinois.", "Except as otherwise provided herein, the Parties may litigate in court to compel arbitration, stay proceedings pending arbitration, or to confirm, modify, vacate, or enter judgment on the award entered by the arbitrator.", "If for any reason, a Dispute proceeds in court rather than arbitration, the Dispute shall be commenced or prosecuted in the state and federal courts located in Cook County, Illinois, and the Parties hereby consent to, and waive all defenses of lack of personal jurisdiction, and forum non conveniens with respect to venue and jurisdiction in such state and federal courts.", "Application of the United Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods and the Uniform Computer Information Transaction Act (UCITA) are excluded from these Legal Terms.", "In no event shall any Dispute brought by either Party related in any way to the Services be commenced more than one (1) year after the cause of action arose.", "If this provision is found to be illegal or unenforceable, then neither Party will elect to arbitrate any Dispute falling within that portion of this provision found to be illegal or unenforceable and such Dispute shall be decided by a court of competent jurisdiction within the courts listed for jurisdiction above, and the Parties agree to submit to the personal jurisdiction of that court.", "Restrictions. The Parties agree that any arbitration shall be limited to the Dispute between the Parties individually.", "To the full extent permitted by law, (a) no arbitration shall be joined with any other proceeding; (b) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be arbitrated on a class-action basis or to utilize class action procedures; and (c) there is no right or authority for any Dispute to be brought in a purported representative capacity on behalf of the general public or any other persons.", "Exceptions to informal negotiations and arbitration. The Parties agree that the following Disputes are not subject to the above provisions concerning informal negotiations and binding arbitration: (a) any Disputes seeking to enforce or protect, or concerning the validity of, any of the intellectual property rights of a Party; (b) any Dispute related to, or arising from, allegations of theft, piracy, invasion of privacy, or unauthorized use; and (c) any claim for injunctive relief.", "If this provision is found to be illegal or unenforceable, then neither Party will elect to arbitrate any Dispute falling within that portion of this provision found to be illegal or unenforceable and such Dispute shall be decided by a court of competent jurisdiction within the courts listed for jurisdiction above, and the Parties agree to submit to the personal jurisdiction of that court."]}, {"heading": "20. Corrections", "paragraphs": ["There may be information on the Services that contains typographical errors, inaccuracies, or omissions, including descriptions, pricing, availability, and various other information. We reserve the right to correct any errors, inaccuracies, or omissions and to change or update the information on the Services at any time, without prior notice."]}, {"heading": "21. Disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["THE SERVICES ARE PROVIDED ON AN AS-IS AND AS-AVAILABLE BASIS. YOU AGREE THAT YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES WILL BE AT YOUR SOLE RISK. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE DISCLAIM ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, IN CONNECTION WITH THE SERVICES AND YOUR USE THEREOF, INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.", "WE MAKE NO WARRANTIES OR REPRESENTATIONS ABOUT THE ACCURACY OR COMPLETENESS OF THE SERVICES' CONTENT (INCLUDING BOOK DETAILS FROM GOOGLE BOOKS AND SUMMARIES AND ANSWERS WRITTEN BY AI) OR THE CONTENT OF ANY WEBSITES OR MOBILE APPLICATIONS LINKED TO THE SERVICES AND WE WILL ASSUME NO LIABILITY OR RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY:", "(1) ERRORS, MISTAKES, OR INACCURACIES OF CONTENT AND MATERIALS,", "(2) PERSONAL INJURY OR PROPERTY DAMAGE, OF ANY NATURE WHATSOEVER, RESULTING FROM YOUR ACCESS TO AND USE OF THE SERVICES,", "(3) ANY UNAUTHORIZED ACCESS TO OR USE OF OUR SECURE SERVERS AND/OR ANY AND ALL PERSONAL INFORMATION STORED THEREIN,", "(4) ANY INTERRUPTION OR CESSATION OF TRANSMISSION TO OR FROM THE SERVICES,", "(5) ANY BUGS, VIRUSES, TROJAN HORSES, OR THE LIKE WHICH MAY BE TRANSMITTED TO OR THROUGH THE SERVICES BY ANY THIRD PARTY,", "AND/OR (6) ANY ERRORS OR OMISSIONS IN ANY CONTENT AND MATERIALS OR FOR ANY LOSS OR DAMAGE OF ANY KIND INCURRED AS A RESULT OF THE USE OF ANY CONTENT POSTED, TRANSMITTED, OR OTHERWISE MADE AVAILABLE VIA THE SERVICES.", "WE DO NOT WARRANT, ENDORSE, GUARANTEE, OR ASSUME RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY PRODUCT OR SERVICE OFFERED BY A THIRD PARTY THROUGH THE SERVICES OR ANY HYPERLINKED WEBSITE, AND WE WILL NOT BE A PARTY TO OR IN ANY WAY BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MONITORING ANY TRANSACTION BETWEEN YOU AND ANY THIRD-PARTY PROVIDERS OF PRODUCTS OR SERVICES.", "AS WITH THE PURCHASE OF A PRODUCT OR SERVICE THROUGH ANY MEDIUM OR IN ANY ENVIRONMENT, YOU SHOULD USE YOUR BEST JUDGMENT AND EXERCISE CAUTION WHERE APPROPRIATE."]}, {"heading": "22. Limitations of liability", "paragraphs": ["IN NO EVENT WILL WE OR OUR DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AGENTS BE LIABLE TO YOU OR ANY THIRD PARTY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFIT, LOST REVENUE, LOSS OF DATA, OR OTHER DAMAGES ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICES, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.", "NOTWITHSTANDING ANYTHING TO THE CONTRARY CONTAINED HEREIN, OUR LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY CAUSE WHATSOEVER AND REGARDLESS OF THE FORM OF THE ACTION, WILL AT ALL TIMES BE LIMITED TO THE AMOUNT PAID, IF ANY, BY YOU TO US DURING THE SIX (6) MONTH PERIOD PRIOR TO ANY CAUSE OF ACTION ARISING.", "CERTAIN US STATE LAWS AND INTERNATIONAL LAWS DO NOT ALLOW LIMITATIONS ON IMPLIED WARRANTIES OR THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF CERTAIN DAMAGES. IF THESE LAWS APPLY TO YOU, SOME OR ALL OF THE ABOVE DISCLAIMERS OR LIMITATIONS MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU, AND YOU MAY HAVE ADDITIONAL RIGHTS."]}, {"heading": "23. Indemnification", "paragraphs": ["You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold us harmless, including our subsidiaries, affiliates, and all of our respective officers, agents, partners, and employees, from and against any loss, damage, liability, claim, or demand, including reasonable attorneys' fees and expenses, made by any third party due to or arising out of:", "(1) your Contributions;", "(2) use of the Services;", "(3) breach of these Legal Terms;", "(4) any breach of your representations and warranties set forth in these Legal Terms;", "(5) your violation of the rights of a third party, including but not limited to intellectual property rights;", "or (6) any overt harmful act toward any other user of the Services with whom you connected via the Services.", "Notwithstanding the foregoing, we reserve the right, at your expense, to assume the exclusive defense and control of any matter for which you are required to indemnify us, and you agree to cooperate, at your expense, with our defense of such claims. We will use reasonable efforts to notify you of any such claim, action, or proceeding which is subject to this indemnification upon becoming aware of it."]}, {"heading": "24. User data", "paragraphs": ["We will maintain certain data that you transmit to the Services for the purpose of managing the performance of the Services, as well as data relating to your use of the Services, as our Privacy Policy describes. You can download a copy of your data at any time from Account (Download my data).", "To the extent permitted by law, you are responsible for keeping your own copy of anything you can't afford to lose, and you agree that we shall have no liability to you for any loss or corruption of any such data."]}, {"heading": "25. Electronic communications, transactions, and signatures", "paragraphs": ["Visiting the Services, sending us emails, and completing online forms constitute electronic communications. You consent to receive electronic communications, and you agree that all agreements, notices, disclosures, and other communications we provide to you electronically, via email and on the Services, satisfy any legal requirement that such communication be in writing.", "YOU HEREBY AGREE TO THE USE OF ELECTRONIC SIGNATURES, CONTRACTS, ORDERS, AND OTHER RECORDS, AND TO ELECTRONIC DELIVERY OF NOTICES, POLICIES, AND RECORDS OF TRANSACTIONS INITIATED OR COMPLETED BY US OR VIA THE SERVICES.", "You hereby waive any rights or requirements under any statutes, regulations, rules, ordinances, or other laws in any jurisdiction which require an original signature or delivery or retention of non-electronic records, or to payments or the granting of credits by any means other than electronic means."]}, {"heading": "26. SMS text messaging", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm doesn't send text messages (SMS) and doesn't ask for your phone number. If we ever start a text messaging program, we'll add its terms here, including how to opt out, before it begins."]}, {"heading": "27. California users and residents", "paragraphs": ["If any complaint with us is not satisfactorily resolved, you can contact the Complaint Assistance Unit of the Division of Consumer Services of the California Department of Consumer Affairs in writing at 1625 North Market Blvd., Suite N 112, Sacramento, California 95834 or by telephone at (800) 952-5210 or (916) 445-1254."]}, {"heading": "28. Miscellaneous", "paragraphs": ["These Legal Terms and any policies or operating rules posted by us on the Services or in respect to the Services constitute the entire agreement and understanding between you and us. Our failure to exercise or enforce any right or provision of these Legal Terms shall not operate as a waiver of such right or provision. These Legal Terms operate to the fullest extent permissible by law.", "We may assign any or all of our rights and obligations to others at any time. We shall not be responsible or liable for any loss, damage, delay, or failure to act caused by any cause beyond our reasonable control.", "If any provision or part of a provision of these Legal Terms is determined to be unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that provision or part of the provision is deemed severable from these Legal Terms and does not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions.", "There is no joint venture, partnership, employment or agency relationship created between you and us as a result of these Legal Terms or use of the Services. You agree that these Legal Terms will not be construed against us by virtue of having drafted them.", "You hereby waive any and all defenses you may have based on the electronic form of these Legal Terms and the lack of signing by the parties hereto to execute these Legal Terms."]}, {"heading": "29. Your account", "paragraphs": ["Account holders must be 18 or older. You may add profiles for people in your household, including Kids profiles with your consent, and you're responsible for how they're used.", "Keep your password private. You can change it, and delete your account, from Account at any time."]}, {"heading": "30. Membership", "paragraphs": ["Plans renew automatically each month on your billing day until you cancel, which you can do online at any time; reading continues until the end of the period you've paid for. Cancel at least 48 hours before your billing date to stop the next charge; cancelling later means one more monthly charge, and then the membership ends. No refunds.", "You can change your billing day (the 1st to the 28th), and pause and resume, from Account. Yearly plans cost ten times the monthly price, start the day you pay and renew on that date each year until you cancel; we remind you in the app 30 days before. The same 48 hours' notice applies, so cancelling later means one more yearly charge.", "Moving from monthly to yearly starts the year at once, with the unused part of the month taken off its price; moving a yearly plan to a bigger plan charges the difference for the rest of the year straight away, and to a smaller one takes effect at renewal with no credit. Yearly plans can't be paused or change their billing day.", "You can choose monthly billing at any time, and it starts on your renewal date, with nothing charged or refunded before then.", "This is not a demo app anymore: your LiteraryWorm account is a live account. You'll be billed monthly, or yearly if you choose, until you cancel. Add a payment method in Account → Plan and billing to continue your membership. On monthly billing you can change your billing day to any day from the 1st to the 28th, and start, pause or cancel billing at any time in Account; a yearly plan can be cancelled at any time, but not paused.", "Plan limits. Each plan includes the audiobook listening, profiles and offline devices shown on the Plans page: Basic, 5 hours a month, 1 profile and 1 device; Standard, 30 hours, 3 profiles and 10 devices; Premium, unlimited listening, 12 profiles and 24 devices. Listening is counted for the whole household on every device.", "When a month's hours are used up, audiobooks pause until the 1st of the next month; reading carries on, and you can change plan at any time. To move to a plan with fewer profiles or offline devices, first set aside or remove the profiles and free the devices it has no room for.", "A household that already has more profiles than its plan now allows, because the plan changed, keeps them in use but can't add more until it fits. A profile set aside keeps its shelf, history and settings, doesn't count towards the plan, and comes back when there's room. While a yearly membership waits to move to a smaller plan at renewal, it has that plan's room already.", "Each device that saves books with Read offline holds one of the plan's places: free one in Account → Plan and billing to use another device, and the freed device's offline books are removed the next time it opens LiteraryWorm.", "Staff memberships. People with a LiteraryWorm staff role (admin, editor, developer, billing, customer service, blog or sales) have a complimentary Premium membership for as long as they hold a role. It's never billed and can't be paused or cancelled; it ends when their last staff role is removed, and they can then choose a plan like any member."]}, {"heading": "31. Your licence to read and listen", "paragraphs": ["While your membership is active, we give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to read and listen to the books in LiteraryWorm for your own and your household's non-commercial use, in the app.", "You may not copy, sell, share, broadcast or publicly perform the books, remove or get around any protection on them, or use them to train AI models. Books saved for offline reading stay in the app on your device.", "This licence doesn't apply to public-domain works themselves, which anyone may use freely; it covers our app, our edition and our service."]}, {"heading": "32. Who owns the books and the app", "paragraphs": ["Public-domain titles: the texts come from Project Gutenberg and the recordings from LibriVox, whose volunteers release their recordings into the public domain. These works are in the public domain in the United States; they may not be everywhere, so check your country's rules before using them outside LiteraryWorm.", "Other LiteraryWorm titles show sample pages, not the published books. Book details and covers from Google Books belong to their publishers and rights holders and are shown under Google's terms.", "Summaries, Ask the book answers, Who's who and chapter quizzes are written by AI (and so are Previously… recaps) (Claude) and labelled so. They may be wrong; they're provided for your own reading and may not be republished as LiteraryWorm's.", "The LiteraryWorm name, logo, design and software belong to LiteraryWorm. Using the service doesn't give you any rights in them beyond these Terms."]}, {"heading": "33. What you post, and the license you give us", "paragraphs": ["You own what you write: reading logs, club posts, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights.", "So we can run the features you use, you give LiteraryWorm a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to store, copy and display what you post, only where and to whom you posted it (logs on the book's public page with your display name, club posts to the club, shared lists to anyone with the link). The licence ends when you delete the content or your account, except for copies already made by others, such as someone else's screenshot.", "Notes, highlights, saved words and private lists are never shown to anyone else."]}, {"heading": "34. Books you upload", "paragraphs": ["Upload only books you have the right to read in this way, such as DRM-free books you've bought or works in the public domain. Don't upload books you don't have rights to, and don't remove DRM to upload them.", "Your uploads stay private to the profile that added them. We store their text only to show it to you, claim no rights in them, and delete them when you do or when you delete the profile or account.", "You can start a book club around a book you uploaded. Its members see only the title and author; each of them reads their own copy, which they must also have the right to read, and nobody's upload is shared with anyone else."]}, {"heading": "35. Rules, changes and ending", "paragraphs": ["Don't post anything unlawful, hateful, harassing or infringing, impersonate others, spam clubs, or try to break or overload the service. We may remove content that breaks these rules and suspend accounts that keep doing so, including repeat copyright infringers (see Copyright/DMCA).", "LiteraryWorm is provided as is. We'll tell you before changing these Terms in ways that matter, and you can cancel or delete your account at any time."]}, {"heading": "36. Contact us", "paragraphs": ["In order to resolve a complaint regarding the Services or to receive further information regarding use of the Services, please contact us at: LiteraryWorm, support@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["This License Agreement covers the LiteraryWorm app itself, in your browser or installed from it. Our Terms of Service cover your membership, and where both cover the same thing, the Terms of Service apply.", "You may use the app on your own devices for yourself and your household. Don't copy, change, resell or take apart the app, or use it to break the law or anyone's rights.", "We look after the app and its updates, and you can reach us at support@literaryworm.com."]}, {"heading": "1. The application", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm (\"Licensed Application\") is a piece of software created to read and listen to books online. It runs in a web browser and can be installed from the browser on phones, tablets and computers (\"Devices\"). It is used to read ebooks and listen to audiobooks, keep a library and goals for each person at home, read along with book clubs, and review books and share opinions with other readers.", "The books we offer in full are in the public domain and have no DRM. Members can also read DRM-free EPUBs they upload.", "The Licensed Application is not tailored to comply with industry-specific regulations (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA), Federal Information Security Management Act (FISMA), etc.), so if your interactions would be subjected to such laws, you may not use this Licensed Application. You may not use the Licensed Application in a way that would violate the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act (GLBA).", "The Licensed Application isn't sold through an app store, and no app store or other third party is a party to this License Agreement. LiteraryWorm is solely responsible for the Licensed Application and its content."]}, {"heading": "2. Scope of license", "paragraphs": ["2.1 You are given a non-transferable, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable license to use the Licensed Application on any Devices that You (End-User) own or control, with the exception that people in your household may use it through the profiles on your account, as the Terms of Service allow.", "2.2 This license will also govern any updates of the Licensed Application provided by Licensor that replace, repair, and/or supplement the first Licensed Application, unless a separate license is provided for such update, in which case the terms of that new license will govern.", "2.3 You may not share or make the Licensed Application available to third parties (except through features the Licensed Application offers, such as shared lists and book clubs, or with LiteraryWorm's prior written consent), sell, rent, lend, lease or otherwise redistribute the Licensed Application.", "2.4 You may not reverse engineer, translate, disassemble, integrate, decompile, remove, modify, combine, create derivative works or updates of, adapt, or attempt to derive the source code of the Licensed Application, or any part thereof, except with LiteraryWorm's prior written consent or where the law allows it. Being able to see source code we publish doesn't give You a license to use it.", "2.5 You may not copy (excluding when expressly authorized by this license) or alter the Licensed Application or portions thereof. Books You save for offline reading are kept in the Licensed Application on that Device only. You may not remove any intellectual property notices. If you sell or give away a Device, sign out of LiteraryWorm on it first; signing out removes books you uploaded from that Device, and you can clear books saved for offline from the Licensed Application or your browser.", "2.6 Violations of the obligations mentioned above, as well as the attempt of such infringement, may be subject to prosecution and damages.", "2.7 Licensor reserves the right to modify the terms and conditions of licensing. We'll tell you before changing them in ways that matter.", "2.8 Nothing in this license should be interpreted to restrict third-party terms. When using the Licensed Application, You must ensure that You comply with applicable third-party terms and conditions."]}, {"heading": "3. Technical requirements", "paragraphs": ["3.1 The Licensed Application requires a current version of Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari and an internet connection, except for books saved for offline reading. Licensor recommends keeping your browser up to date.", "3.2 Licensor attempts to keep the Licensed Application updated so that it works with new versions of browsers and new hardware. You are not granted rights to claim such an update.", "3.3 You acknowledge that it is Your responsibility to confirm and determine that the Device on which You intend to use the Licensed Application satisfies the technical specifications mentioned above.", "3.4 Licensor reserves the right to modify the technical specifications as it sees appropriate at any time."]}, {"heading": "4. Maintenance and support", "paragraphs": ["4.1 The Licensor is solely responsible for providing any maintenance and support services for this Licensed Application. You can reach the Licensor at support@literaryworm.com.", "4.2 No app store or other third party has any obligation to provide maintenance and support services for the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "5. Use of data", "paragraphs": ["You acknowledge that Licensor stores and can access Your account, Your profiles and what You read, save and share in the Licensed Application, so that it can provide it to You, and that Licensor's use of that information is subject to Your legal agreements with Licensor and Licensor's privacy policy: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/privacy.", "You acknowledge that the Licensor and its hosting providers may collect technical data, such as your browser type, IP address and error reports, to keep the Licensed Application secure and working and to offer product support, and a short label for each Device you're signed in on (such as \"Chrome on Windows\") so you can send a book to another Device. Licensor doesn't use this information for advertising."]}, {"heading": "6. User-generated contributions", "paragraphs": ["The Licensed Application invites you to contribute content: reading logs (shown on a book's public page with your display name), book club posts (seen by the club's members), ratings, lists you choose to share by link, and private notes and highlights (collectively, \"Contributions\"). Contributions you make public may be viewable by anyone, including through links shared outside the Licensed Application. When you create or make available any Contributions, you thereby represent and warrant that:", "1. The creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party.", "2. You are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Licensed Application, and other users of the Licensed Application to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Licensed Application and this License Agreement.", "3. You have the written consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Licensed Application and this License Agreement.", "4. Your Contributions are not false, inaccurate, or misleading.", "5. Your Contributions are not unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation.", "6. Your Contributions are not obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, or otherwise objectionable (as determined by us).", "7. Your Contributions do not ridicule, mock, disparage, intimidate, or abuse anyone.", "8. Your Contributions are not used to harass or threaten (in the legal sense of those terms) any other person and to promote violence against a specific person or class of people.", "9. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law, regulation, or rule.", "10. Your Contributions do not violate the privacy or publicity rights of any third party.", "11. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law concerning child sexual abuse material, or otherwise intended to protect the health or well-being of minors.", "12. Your Contributions do not include any offensive comments that are connected to race, national origin, gender, sexual preference, or physical handicap.", "13. Your Contributions do not otherwise violate, or link to material that violates, any provision of this License Agreement, or any applicable law or regulation.", "Any use of the Licensed Application in violation of the foregoing violates this License Agreement and may result in, among other things, termination or suspension of your rights to use the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "7. Contribution license", "paragraphs": ["You own your Contributions. By posting them, you give LiteraryWorm the license described in the Terms of Service (\"What you post, and the licence you give us\"): a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to store, copy and display your Contributions, only where and to whom you posted them, so we can run the features you use.", "The license ends when you delete the Contribution or your account, except for copies already made by others. Notes, highlights, saved words and private lists are never shown to anyone else.", "We are not liable for any statements or representations in your Contributions. You are solely responsible for your Contributions to the Licensed Application and you expressly agree to exonerate us from any and all responsibility and to refrain from any legal action against us regarding your Contributions.", "We may remove Contributions that break this License Agreement or the Terms of Service, at any time and without notice. We have no obligation to monitor your Contributions."]}, {"heading": "8. Liability", "paragraphs": ["8.1 Licensor's responsibility in the case of violation of obligations and tort shall be limited to intent and gross negligence. Only in case of a breach of essential contractual duties (cardinal obligations), Licensor shall also be liable in case of slight negligence. In any case, liability shall be limited to the foreseeable, contractually typical damages. The limitation mentioned above does not apply to injuries to life, limb, or health.", "8.2 Licensor takes no accountability or responsibility for any damages caused due to a breach of duties according to Section 2 of this License Agreement. To avoid data loss, You can download a copy of your data at any time from Account (Download my data). You are aware that in case of alterations or manipulations of the Licensed Application, You may not have access to the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "9. Warranty", "paragraphs": ["9.1 Licensor warrants that the Licensed Application is free of spyware, trojan horses, viruses, or any other malware at the time You use it. Licensor warrants that the Licensed Application works as described in Help.", "9.2 No warranty is provided for the Licensed Application that is not executable on the Device, that has been unauthorizedly modified, handled inappropriately or culpably, combined or installed with inappropriate hardware or software, used with inappropriate accessories, regardless if by Yourself or by third parties, or if there are any other reasons outside of LiteraryWorm's sphere of influence that affect the executability of the Licensed Application.", "9.3 Please notify LiteraryWorm about issues You discover without delay by email at support@literaryworm.com. The defect report will be taken into consideration and further investigated if it has been emailed within a period of seven (7) days after discovery.", "9.4 If we confirm that the Licensed Application is defective, LiteraryWorm reserves a choice to remedy the situation either by means of solving the defect or substitute delivery.", "9.5 Payments for LiteraryWorm memberships are non-refundable, as our Return Policy explains (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/returns).", "9.6 If the user is an entrepreneur, any claim based on faults expires after a statutory period of limitation amounting to twelve (12) months after the Licensed Application was made available to the user. The statutory periods of limitation given by law apply for users who are consumers."]}, {"heading": "10. Product claims", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is responsible for addressing any claims of the End-User or any third party relating to the Licensed Application or the End-User's possession and/or use of that Licensed Application, including, but not limited to: (i) product liability claims; (ii) any claim that the Licensed Application fails to conform to any applicable legal or regulatory requirement; and (iii) claims arising under consumer protection, privacy, or similar legislation."]}, {"heading": "11. Legal compliance", "paragraphs": ["You represent and warrant that You are not located in a country that is subject to a US Government embargo, or that has been designated by the US Government as a \"terrorist supporting\" country; and that You are not listed on any US Government list of prohibited or restricted parties."]}, {"heading": "12. Contact information", "paragraphs": ["For general inquiries, complaints, questions or claims concerning the Licensed Application, please email support@literaryworm.com."]}, {"heading": "13. Termination", "paragraphs": ["The license is valid until terminated by LiteraryWorm or by You. You can end it at any time by deleting your account from Account. Your rights under this license will terminate automatically and without notice from LiteraryWorm if You fail to adhere to any term(s) of this license. Upon License termination, You shall stop all use of the Licensed Application, and remove it and any books saved for offline reading from Your Devices."]}, {"heading": "14. Third-party terms of agreements", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm represents and warrants that LiteraryWorm will comply with applicable third-party terms of agreement when using the Licensed Application, including those of the services it relies on: Supabase, Vercel, Mailgun, Anthropic, Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg."]}, {"heading": "15. Intellectual property rights", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm and the End-User acknowledge that, in the event of any third-party claim that the Licensed Application or the End-User's possession and use of that Licensed Application infringes on the third party's intellectual property rights, LiteraryWorm will be solely responsible for the investigation, defense, settlement, and discharge of any such intellectual property infringement claims. Who owns the books and the app is set out in the Terms of Service."]}, {"heading": "16. Applicable law", "paragraphs": ["This License Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Illinois excluding its conflicts of law rules."]}, {"heading": "17. Miscellaneous", "paragraphs": ["17.1 If any of the terms of this agreement should be or become invalid, the validity of the remaining provisions shall not be affected. Invalid terms will be replaced by valid ones formulated in a way that will achieve the primary purpose.", "17.2 Collateral agreements, changes and amendments are only valid if laid down in writing. The preceding clause can only be waived in writing."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$LiteraryWorm is licensed to You (End-User) by LiteraryWorm ("Licensor"), for use only under the terms of this License Agreement. By using the Licensed Application at https://www.literaryworm.com, or installing it on a device from your browser, and any update to it, You agree to be bound by all of the terms and conditions of this License Agreement. It sits alongside our Terms of Service; where they cover the same thing, the Terms of Service apply.$lw$ then $lw$LiteraryWorm is licensed to You (End-User) by LiteraryWorm ("Licensor"), for use only under the terms of this License Agreement. By using the Licensed Application at https://www.literaryworm.com, or installing it on a device from your browser, and any update to it, You agree to be bound by all of the terms and conditions of this License Agreement. It sits alongside our Terms of Service; where they cover the same thing, the Terms of Service apply.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
