 intend to use the Licensed Application satisfies the technical specifications mentioned above.", "3.4 Licensor reserves the right to modify the technical specifications as it sees appropriate at any time."]}, {"heading": "4. Maintenance and support", "paragraphs": ["4.1 The Licensor is solely responsible for providing any maintenance and support services for this Licensed Application. You can reach the Licensor at support@literaryworm.com.", "4.2 No app store or other third party has any obligation to provide maintenance and support services for the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "5. Use of data", "paragraphs": ["You acknowledge that Licensor stores and can access Your account, Your profiles and what You read, save and share in the Licensed Application, so that it can provide it to You, and that Licensor's use of that information is subject to Your legal agreements with Licensor and Licensor's privacy policy: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/privacy.", "You acknowledge that the Licensor and its hosting providers may collect technical data, such as your browser type, IP address and error reports, to keep the Licensed Application secure and working and to offer product support, and a short label for each Device you're signed in on (such as \"Chrome on Windows\") so you can send a book to another Device. Licensor doesn't use this information for advertising."]}, {"heading": "6. User-generated contributions", "paragraphs": ["The Licensed Application invites you to contribute content: reading logs (shown on a book's public page with your display name), book club posts (seen by the club's members), ratings, lists you choose to share by link, and private notes and highlights (collectively, \"Contributions\"). Contributions you make public may be viewable by anyone, including through links shared outside the Licensed Application. When you create or make available any Contributions, you thereby represent and warrant that:", "1. The creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party.", "2. You are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Licensed Application, and other users of the Licensed Application to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Licensed Application and this License Agreement.", "3. You have the written consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Licensed Application and this License Agreement.", "4. Your Contributions are not false, inaccurate, or misleading.", "5. Your Contributions are not unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation.", "6. Your Contributions are not obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, or otherwise objectionable (as determined by us).", "7. Your Contributions do not ridicule, mock, disparage, intimidate, or abuse anyone.", "8. Your Contributions are not used to harass or threaten (in the legal sense of those terms) any other person and to promote violence against a specific person or class of people.", "9. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law, regulation, or rule.", "10. Your Contributions do not violate the privacy or publicity rights of any third party.", "11. Your Contributions do not violate any applicable law concerning child sexual abuse material, or otherwise intended to protect the health or well-being of minors.", "12. Your Contributions do not include any offensive comments that are connected to race, national origin, gender, sexual preference, or physical handicap.", "13. Your Contributions do not otherwise violate, or link to material that violates, any provision of this License Agreement, or any applicable law or regulation.", "Any use of the Licensed Application in violation of the foregoing violates this License Agreement and may result in, among other things, termination or suspension of your rights to use the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "7. Contribution license", "paragraphs": ["You own your Contributions. By posting them, you give LiteraryWorm the license described in the Terms of Service (\"What you post, and the licence you give us\"): a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to store, copy and display your Contributions, only where and to whom you posted them, so we can run the features you use.", "The license ends when you delete the Contribution or your account, except for copies already made by others. Notes, highlights, saved words and private lists are never shown to anyone else.", "We are not liable for any statements or representations in your Contributions. You are solely responsible for your Contributions to the Licensed Application and you expressly agree to exonerate us from any and all responsibility and to refrain from any legal action against us regarding your Contributions.", "We may remove Contributions that break this License Agreement or the Terms of Service, at any time and without notice. We have no obligation to monitor your Contributions."]}, {"heading": "8. Liability", "paragraphs": ["8.1 Licensor's responsibility in the case of violation of obligations and tort shall be limited to intent and gross negligence. Only in case of a breach of essential contractual duties (cardinal obligations), Licensor shall also be liable in case of slight negligence. In any case, liability shall be limited to the foreseeable, contractually typical damages. The limitation mentioned above does not apply to injuries to life, limb, or health.", "8.2 Licensor takes no accountability or responsibility for any damages caused due to a breach of duties according to Section 2 of this License Agreement. To avoid data loss, You can download a copy of your data at any time from Account (Download my data). You are aware that in case of alterations or manipulations of the Licensed Application, You may not have access to the Licensed Application."]}, {"heading": "9. Warranty", "paragraphs": ["9.1 Licensor warrants that the Licensed Application is free of spyware, trojan horses, viruses, or any other malware at the time You use it. Licensor warrants that the Licensed Application works as described in Help.", "9.2 No warranty is provided for the Licensed Application that is not executable on the Device, that has been unauthorizedly modified, handled inappropriately or culpably, combined or installed with inappropriate hardware or software, used with inappropriate accessories, regardless if by Yourself or by third parties, or if there are any other reasons outside of LiteraryWorm's sphere of influence that affect the executability of the Licensed Application.", "9.3 Please notify LiteraryWorm about issues You discover without delay by email at support@literaryworm.com. The defect report will be taken into consideration and further investigated if it has been emailed within a period of seven (7) days after discovery.", "9.4 If we confirm that the Licensed Application is defective, LiteraryWorm reserves a choice to remedy the situation either by means of solving the defect or substitute delivery.", "9.5 Payments for LiteraryWorm memberships are non-refundable, as our Return Policy explains (https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/returns).", "9.6 If the user is an entrepreneur, any claim based on faults expires after a statutory period of limitation amounting to twelve (12) months after the Licensed Application was made available to the user. The statutory periods of limitation given by law apply for users who are consumers."]}, {"heading": "10. Product claims", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is responsible for addressing any claims of the End-User or any third party relating to the Licensed Application or the End-User's possession and/or use of that Licensed Application, including, but not limited to: (i) product liability claims; (ii) any claim that the Licensed Application fails to conform to any applicable legal or regulatory requirement; and (iii) claims arising under consumer protection, privacy, or similar legislation."]}, {"heading": "11. Legal compliance", "paragraphs": ["You represent and warrant that You are not located in a country that is subject to a US Government embargo, or that has been designated by the US Government as a \"terrorist supporting\" country; and that You are not listed on any US Government list of prohibited or restricted parties."]}, {"heading": "12. Contact information", "paragraphs": ["For general inquiries, complaints, questions or claims concerning the Licensed Application, please email support@literaryworm.com."]}, {"heading": "13. Termination", "paragraphs": ["The license is valid until terminated by LiteraryWorm or by You. You can end it at any time by deleting your account from Account. Your rights under this license will terminate automatically and without notice from LiteraryWorm if You fail to adhere to any term(s) of this license. Upon License termination, You shall stop all use of the Licensed Application, and remove it and any books saved for offline reading from Your Devices."]}, {"heading": "14. Third-party terms of agreements", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm represents and warrants that LiteraryWorm will comply with applicable third-party terms of agreement when using the Licensed Application, including those of the services it relies on: Supabase, Vercel, Mailgun, Anthropic, Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg."]}, {"heading": "15. Intellectual property rights", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm and the End-User acknowledge that, in the event of any third-party claim that the Licensed Application or the End-User's possession and use of that Licensed Application infringes on the third party's intellectual property rights, LiteraryWorm will be solely responsible for the investigation, defense, settlement, and discharge of any such intellectual property infringement claims. Who owns the books and the app is set out in the Terms of Service."]}, {"heading": "16. Applicable law", "paragraphs": ["This License Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Illinois excluding its conflicts of law rules."]}, {"heading": "17. Miscellaneous", "paragraphs": ["17.1 If any of the terms of this agreement should be or become invalid, the validity of the remaining provisions shall not be affected. Invalid terms will be replaced by valid ones formulated in a way that will achieve the primary purpose.", "17.2 Collateral agreements, changes and amendments are only valid if laid down in writing. The preceding clause can only be waived in writing."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["Use LiteraryWorm lawfully and kindly. Don't harass anyone, post anything illegal or hateful, upload books you don't have the right to read, or try to break or overload the Services.", "Use the AI features as reading aids, and don't try to make them produce harmful content. Reading logs and reviews should be honest and your own.", "Report anything that breaks this Policy to report@literaryworm.com. We may remove content or suspend accounts that break it."]}, {"heading": "Agreement to this policy", "paragraphs": ["When you use the AI-powered services provided by LiteraryWorm (\"AI Products\"), you warrant that you will comply with this document, our Legal Terms and all applicable laws and regulations governing AI. Our AI Products are book summaries, content notes, Ask the book, Translate, Who's who, chapter quizzes and Previously… recaps. They're written by Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic, and labelled as written by AI.", "Your usage of our AI Products signifies your agreement to engage with our platform in a lawful, ethical, and responsible manner that respects the rights and dignity of all individuals. If you do not agree with these Legal Terms, please refrain from using our Services. Your continued use of our Services implies acceptance of these Legal Terms.", "Please carefully review this Policy which applies to any and all:", "(a) uses of our Services (as defined in \"Legal Terms\");", "(b) forms, materials, consent tools, comments, posts, and all other content available on the Services (\"Content\");", "(c) material which you contribute to the Services, including any upload, post, reading log, rating, book club post, shared list or comment (\"Contribution\");", "(d) responsible implementation and management of AI Products within our Services."]}, {"heading": "Who we are", "paragraphs": ["We are LiteraryWorm (\"Company,\" \"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our\"). We operate the website https://www.literaryworm.com (the \"Site\"), as well as any other related products and services that refer or link to this Policy (collectively, the \"Services\")."]}, {"heading": "Use of the Services", "paragraphs": ["When you use the Services, you warrant that you will comply with this Policy and with all applicable laws.", "You also acknowledge that you may not:", "1. Systematically retrieve data or other content from the Services to create or compile, directly or indirectly, a collection, compilation, database, or directory without written permission from us.", "2. Make any unauthorized use of the Services, including collecting display names and/or email addresses of users by electronic or other means for the purpose of sending unsolicited email, or creating user accounts by automated means or under false pretenses.", "3. Circumvent, disable, or otherwise interfere with security-related features of the Services, including features that prevent or restrict the use or copying of any Content or enforce limitations on the use of the Services and/or the Content contained therein, such as profile PINs, daily reading limits and age ratings.", "4. Engage in unauthorized framing of or linking to the Services.", "5. Trick, defraud, or mislead us and other users, especially in any attempt to learn sensitive account information such as user passwords.", "6. Make improper use of our Services, including our support services, or submit false reports of abuse or misconduct.", "7. Engage in any automated use of the Services, such as using scripts to send comments or messages, or using any data mining, robots, or similar data gathering and extraction tools.", "8. Interfere with, disrupt, or create an undue burden on the Services or the networks or services connected to the Services.", "9. Attempt to impersonate another user or person or use the display name of another user.", "10. Use any information obtained from the Services in order to harass, abuse, or harm another person.", "11. Use the Services as part of any effort to compete with us or otherwise use the Services and/or the Content for any revenue-generating endeavor or commercial enterprise.", "12. Decipher, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer any of the software comprising or in any way making up a part of the Services, except as expressly permitted by applicable law.", "13. Attempt to bypass any measures of the Services designed to prevent or restrict access to the Services, or any portion of the Services.", "14. Harass, annoy, intimidate, or threaten any of our employees or agents engaged in providing any portion of the Services to you.", "15. Delete the copyright or other proprietary rights notice from any Content.", "16. Copy or adapt the Services' software, including but not limited to HTML, JavaScript, or other code.", "17. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) viruses, Trojan horses, or other material, including excessive use of capital letters and spamming (continuous posting of repetitive text), that interferes with any party's uninterrupted use and enjoyment of the Services or modifies, impairs, disrupts, alters, or interferes with the use, features, functions, operation, or maintenance of the Services.", "18. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) any material that acts as a passive or active information collection or transmission mechanism, including without limitation, clear graphics interchange formats (\"gifs\"), 1×1 pixels, web bugs, cookies, or other similar devices (sometimes referred to as \"spyware\" or \"passive collection mechanisms\" or \"pcms\").", "19. Except as may be the result of standard search engine or Internet browser usage, or the Services' own Read offline feature, use, launch, develop, or distribute any automated system, including without limitation, any spider, robot, cheat utility, scraper, or offline reader that accesses the Services, or use or launch any unauthorized script or other software.", "20. Disparage, tarnish, or otherwise harm, in our opinion, us and/or the Services.", "21. Use the Services in a manner inconsistent with any applicable laws or regulations.", "22. Use a buying agent or purchasing agent to make purchases on the Services.", "23. Sell or otherwise transfer your account or a profile."]}, {"heading": "Subscriptions", "paragraphs": ["If you subscribe to our Services, you understand, acknowledge, and agree that you may not, except if expressly permitted:", "1. Engage in any use, including modification, copying, redistribution, publication, display, performance, or retransmission, of any portions of any Services, other than as expressly permitted by this Policy, without the prior written consent of LiteraryWorm, which consent LiteraryWorm may grant or refuse in its sole and absolute discretion.", "2. Reconstruct or attempt to discover any source code or algorithms of the Services, or any portion thereof, by any means whatsoever. Being able to see source code we publish doesn't give you a license to use it.", "3. Provide, or otherwise make available, the Services to any third party, other than the people in your household who use the profiles on your account.", "4. Intercept any data not intended for you.", "5. Damage, reveal, or alter any user's data, or any other hardware, software, or information relating to another person or entity."]}, {"heading": "AI Products", "paragraphs": ["When you use the AI Products provided by LiteraryWorm, you warrant that you will not:", "1. Try to make the AI Products produce content that this Policy forbids, or that breaks Anthropic's usage policies.", "2. Deploy AI techniques that utilize subliminal, manipulative, or deceptive methods designed to distort behavior and impair informed decision-making, particularly when such actions cause significant harm to individuals.", "3. Exploit vulnerabilities related to age, disability, or socio-economic circumstances through AI in a way that distorts behavior or decision-making, especially if this results in significant harm to the individual.", "4. Use AI systems for biometric categorization that infer sensitive attributes such as race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life, or sexual orientation, except in limited cases, such as labeling or filtering lawfully acquired datasets, or specific law enforcement activities.", "5. Implement AI-based social scoring systems that evaluate or classify individuals or groups based on their social behavior or personal traits in a manner that causes harm, discrimination, or unfair treatment.", "6. Assess the risk of an individual committing criminal offenses based solely on profiling, personality traits, or other non-behavioral factors, except in narrowly defined circumstances where legal safeguards are in place.", "7. Compile facial recognition databases through untargeted scraping of facial images from the internet, social media, or CCTV footage, unless it is part of a legally compliant and narrowly defined purpose.", "8. Use AI to infer emotions in sensitive environments such as workplaces, educational institutions, or any other context where such analysis could lead to discrimination, unfair treatment, or privacy violations.", "9. Engage in real-time remote biometric identification in public places for law enforcement purposes, except in specific situations where there are strong legal justifications and oversight mechanisms."]}, {"heading": "Artificial intelligence", "paragraphs": ["We recognize the significant impact AI can have on our users and society, and we are dedicated to ensuring that our AI Products are designed and operated in a manner that aligns with comprehensive ethical standards. We aim to use AI to enhance user experiences while upholding fairness, transparency, and accountability principles.", "That's why everything our AI Products write is labelled as written by AI, and why Ask the book and Who's who are only given the text up to your place in the book, and a quiz only the chapter it's about. A Previously… recap gets only the chapters before yours. Translate is given only the words you selected, and content notes only the book's details.", "This Policy applies to all AI-powered features, services, and systems in our Services. It governs the development, deployment, and use of AI technologies to protect users' rights and maintain transparency in all AI operations. This Policy applies to all stakeholders, including employees, third-party vendors, and partners who contribute to or interact with our AI Products.", "Enforcement. Any misuse of our AI Products or failure to adhere to the standards outlined in this Policy will result in appropriate actions to ensure the integrity of our platform and the protection of our users. The specific consequences for misuse of AI may vary depending on the nature and severity of the violation and the user's history with our Services.", "Violations may include, but are not limited to:", "1. Engaging the AI Products in ways that violate user privacy, manipulate data, disregard ethical guidelines, or are against AI service providers' terms of use (for our AI Products, Anthropic's).", "2. Deploying AI in a manner that introduces or causes bias, leading to unfair treatment of users or groups.", "3. Improper handling, storage, or use of data by AI Products, leading to breaches of user trust and legal compliance.", "4. Using AI in a way that compromises the privacy and security of our systems, data, or users.", "Depending on the violation, LiteraryWorm may take one or more of the following actions:", "Warnings: The responsible party may receive a formal warning and be required to cease violating practices.", "Temporary Suspension: In cases of repeated or more severe violations, the responsible individual's access to AI Products or certain features of our platform may be temporarily suspended while the issue is investigated.", "Termination of Access: Serious violations, particularly those that result in harm to users or breach privacy or other regulations, may lead to the permanent termination of access to our AI Products and Services.", "Legal Action: In cases where the misuse of AI leads to significant harm, data breaches, or legal violations, we may pursue legal action against the party responsible. This could include reporting the incident to law enforcement or regulatory bodies.", "Public Disclosure: For incidents that impact public trust or involve severe ethical breaches, we reserve the right to publicly disclose the violation and the actions taken in response to maintain transparency and accountability.", "Commitment to Responsible AI. In addition to the consequences outlined above, we are deeply committed to repairing any harm caused by the misuse of AI. This commitment is a testament to our dedication to our users and our responsibility as a company. We will correct biased outcomes and implement additional safeguards to prevent future violations.", "At LiteraryWorm, we are committed to the ongoing refinement and enhancement of our Policy. As technology evolves and regulatory environments shift, we recognize the importance of keeping our policies up to date to ensure that they remain relevant, effective, and aligned with best practices in AI ethics.", "We will regularly review and update our Policy to reflect technological advancements and legal changes in local, national, and international regulations related to AI. Our Policy will be updated as needed to comply with new laws and guidelines, ensuring that our practices remain legally sound and socially responsible."]}, {"heading": "Contributions", "paragraphs": ["In this Policy, the term \"Contributions\" means: any data, information, text, messages or other materials that you post, share, upload, submit, or otherwise provide in any manner on or through the Services, such as reading logs, ratings, book club posts, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights, and books you upload; or any other content, materials, or data you provide to LiteraryWorm or use with the Services.", "Some areas of the Services allow users to upload, transmit, or post Contributions. We may but are under no obligation to review or moderate the Contributions made on the Services, and we expressly exclude our liability for any loss or damage resulting from any of our users' breach of this Policy. Please report any Contribution that you believe breaches this Policy; however, we will determine, in our sole discretion, whether a Contribution is indeed in breach of this Policy.", "You warrant that:", "1. you are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Services, and other users of the Services to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and this Policy;", "2. all your Contributions comply with applicable laws and are original and true (if they represent your opinion or facts);", "3. the creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party; and", "4. you have the verifiable consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and this Policy.", "You also agree that you will not post, transmit, or upload any (or any part of a) Contribution that:", "1. is in breach of applicable laws, regulation, court order, contractual obligation, this Policy, our Legal Terms, a legal duty, or that promotes or facilitates fraud or illegal activities;", "2. is defamatory, obscene, offensive, hateful, insulting, intimidating, bullying, abusive, or threatening, to any person or group;", "3. is false, inaccurate, or misleading;", "4. includes child sexual abuse material, or violates any applicable law intended to protect minors;", "5. contains any material that solicits personal information from anyone under the age of 18 or exploits people under the age of 18 in a sexual or violent manner;", "6. promotes violence, advocates the violent overthrow of any government, or incites, encourages, or threatens physical harm against another;", "7. is obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, contains sexually explicit material, or is otherwise objectionable (as determined by us);", "8. is discriminatory based on race, sex, religion, nationality, disability, sexual orientation, or age;", "9. bullies, intimidates, humiliates, or insults any person;", "10. promotes, facilitates, or assists anyone in promoting and facilitating acts of terrorism;", "11. infringes, or assists anyone in infringing, a third party's intellectual property rights or publicity or privacy rights;", "12. is deceitful, misrepresents your identity or affiliation with any person and/or misleads anyone as to your relationship with us or implies that the Contribution was made by someone else than you;", "13. contains unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation that has been \"paid for,\" whether with monetary compensation or in kind; or", "14. misrepresents your identity or who the Contribution is from."]}, {"heading": "Reviews and ratings", "paragraphs": ["When your Contribution is a review or rating of a book, such as a rating or a reading log, you also agree that:", "1. you have firsthand experience with the book being reviewed;", "2. your Contribution is true to your experience;", "3. you are not affiliated with competitors if posting negative reviews (or linked in any way to, e.g., by being the author or publisher of, a book if posting positive reviews);", "4. you cannot make or offer any conclusions as to the legality of conduct;", "5. you cannot post any false or misleading statements; and", "6. you do not and will not organize a campaign encouraging others to post reviews, whether positive or negative."]}, {"heading": "Reporting a breach of this policy", "paragraphs": ["We may but are under no obligation to review or moderate the Contributions made on the Services and we expressly exclude our liability for any loss or damage resulting from any of our users' breach of this Policy.", "If you consider that any Service, Content, or Contribution breaches this Policy, please email us at report@literaryworm.com to let us know which Service, Content, or Contribution is in breach of this Policy and why.", "If you consider that any Service, Content, or Contribution infringes any third-party intellectual property rights, please email us at report@literaryworm.com. For a formal notice under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, follow the steps on our Copyright/DMCA page.", "You can also send detailed feedback on your interactions with our AI Products by emailing report@literaryworm.com. Please include specific details about the AI interaction, such as the book, the context, the nature of the concern, and any relevant screenshots or documentation.", "We will reasonably determine whether a Service, Content, or Contribution breaches this Policy."]}, {"heading": "Consequences of breaching this policy", "paragraphs": ["The consequences for violating our Policy will vary depending on the severity of the breach and the user's history on the Services, by way of example:", "We may, in some cases, give you a warning and/or remove the infringing Contribution, however, if your breach is serious or if you continue to breach our Legal Terms and this Policy, we have the right to suspend or terminate your access to and use of our Services and, if applicable, disable your account. We may also notify law enforcement or issue legal proceedings against you when we believe that there is a genuine risk to an individual or a threat to public safety.", "We exclude our liability for all action we may take in response to any of your breaches of this Policy."]}, {"heading": "Complaints and removal of legitimate content", "paragraphs": ["If you consider that some Content or Contribution has been mistakenly removed or blocked from the Services, please email us at report@literaryworm.com and we will promptly review our decision to remove such Content or Contribution. The Content or Contribution may stay \"down\" whilst we conduct the review process. If it was removed after a copyright notice, you can also send a counter-notice, as our Copyright/DMCA page explains."]}, {"heading": "Disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is under no obligation to monitor users' activities, and we disclaim any responsibility for any user's misuse of the Services. LiteraryWorm has no responsibility for any user or other Content or Contribution created, maintained, stored, transmitted, or accessible on or through the Services, and is not obligated to monitor or exercise any editorial control over such material.", "If LiteraryWorm becomes aware that any such Content or Contribution violates this Policy, LiteraryWorm may, in addition to removing such Content or Contribution and blocking your account, report such breach to the police or appropriate regulatory authority.", "Unless otherwise stated in this Policy, LiteraryWorm disclaims any obligation to any person who has not entered into an agreement with LiteraryWorm for the use of the Services."]}, {"heading": "How can you contact us about this policy?", "paragraphs": ["If you have any further questions or comments or wish to report any problematic Content or Contribution, you may contact us by email: report@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$This Acceptable Use Policy ("Policy") is part of our Terms of Service ("Legal Terms") and should therefore be read alongside our main Legal Terms: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/terms. It sets out what you may and may not do on LiteraryWorm, what you may post, how to use our AI features responsibly, and how to report anything that breaks it.$lw$ then $lw$This Acceptable Use Policy ("Policy") is part of our Terms of Service ("Legal Terms") and should therefore be read alongside our main Legal Terms: https://www.literaryworm.com/legal/terms. It sets out what you may and may not do on LiteraryWorm, what you may post, how to use our AI features responsibly, and how to report anything that breaks it.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$acceptable-use$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Agreement to this policy", "paragraphs": ["When you use the AI-powered services provided by LiteraryWorm (\"AI Products\"), you warrant that you will comply with this document, our Legal Terms and all applicable laws and regulations governing AI. Our AI Products are the book summaries, Ask the book, Who's who and chapter quizzes and Previously… recaps, which are written by Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic, and labelled as written by AI.", "Your usage of our AI Products signifies your agreement to engage with our platform in a lawful, ethical, and responsible manner that respects the rights and dignity of all individuals. If you do not agree with these Legal Terms, please refrain from using our Services. Your continued use of our Services implies acceptance of these Legal Terms.", "Please carefully review this Policy which applies to any and all:", "(a) uses of our Services (as defined in \"Legal Terms\");", "(b) forms, materials, consent tools, comments, posts, and all other content available on the Services (\"Content\");", "(c) material which you contribute to the Services, including any upload, post, reading log, rating, book club post, shared list or comment (\"Contribution\");", "(d) responsible implementation and management of AI Products within our Services."]}, {"heading": "Who we are", "paragraphs": ["We are LiteraryWorm (\"Company,\" \"we,\" \"us,\" or \"our\"). We operate the website https://www.literaryworm.com (the \"Site\"), as well as any other related products and services that refer or link to this Policy (collectively, the \"Services\")."]}, {"heading": "Use of the Services", "paragraphs": ["When you use the Services, you warrant that you will comply with this Policy and with all applicable laws.", "You also acknowledge that you may not:", "1. Systematically retrieve data or other content from the Services to create or compile, directly or indirectly, a collection, compilation, database, or directory without written permission from us.", "2. Make any unauthorized use of the Services, including collecting display names and/or email addresses of users by electronic or other means for the purpose of sending unsolicited email, or creating user accounts by automated means or under false pretenses.", "3. Circumvent, disable, or otherwise interfere with security-related features of the Services, including features that prevent or restrict the use or copying of any Content or enforce limitations on the use of the Services and/or the Content contained therein, such as profile PINs, daily reading limits and age ratings.", "4. Engage in unauthorized framing of or linking to the Services.", "5. Trick, defraud, or mislead us and other users, especially in any attempt to learn sensitive account information such as user passwords.", "6. Make improper use of our Services, including our support services, or submit false reports of abuse or misconduct.", "7. Engage in any automated use of the Services, such as using scripts to send comments or messages, or using any data mining, robots, or similar data gathering and extraction tools.", "8. Interfere with, disrupt, or create an undue burden on the Services or the networks or services connected to the Services.", "9. Attempt to impersonate another user or person or use the display name of another user.", "10. Use any information obtained from the Services in order to harass, abuse, or harm another person.", "11. Use the Services as part of any effort to compete with us or otherwise use the Services and/or the Content for any revenue-generating endeavor or commercial enterprise.", "12. Decipher, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer any of the software comprising or in any way making up a part of the Services, except as expressly permitted by applicable law.", "13. Attempt to bypass any measures of the Services designed to prevent or restrict access to the Services, or any portion of the Services.", "14. Harass, annoy, intimidate, or threaten any of our employees or agents engaged in providing any portion of the Services to you.", "15. Delete the copyright or other proprietary rights notice from any Content.", "16. Copy or adapt the Services' software, including but not limited to HTML, JavaScript, or other code.", "17. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) viruses, Trojan horses, or other material, including excessive use of capital letters and spamming (continuous posting of repetitive text), that interferes with any party's uninterrupted use and enjoyment of the Services or modifies, impairs, disrupts, alters, or interferes with the use, features, functions, operation, or maintenance of the Services.", "18. Upload or transmit (or attempt to upload or to transmit) any material that acts as a passive or active information collection or transmission mechanism, including without limitation, clear graphics interchange formats (\"gifs\"), 1×1 pixels, web bugs, cookies, or other similar devices (sometimes referred to as \"spyware\" or \"passive collection mechanisms\" or \"pcms\").", "19. Except as may be the result of standard search engine or Internet browser usage, or the Services' own Read offline feature, use, launch, develop, or distribute any automated system, including without limitation, any spider, robot, cheat utility, scraper, or offline reader that accesses the Services, or use or launch any unauthorized script or other software.", "20. Disparage, tarnish, or otherwise harm, in our opinion, us and/or the Services.", "21. Use the Services in a manner inconsistent with any applicable laws or regulations.", "22. Use a buying agent or purchasing agent to make purchases on the Services.", "23. Sell or otherwise transfer your account or a profile."]}, {"heading": "Subscriptions", "paragraphs": ["If you subscribe to our Services, you understand, acknowledge, and agree that you may not, except if expressly permitted:", "1. Engage in any use, including modification, copying, redistribution, publication, display, performance, or retransmission, of any portions of any Services, other than as expressly permitted by this Policy, without the prior written consent of LiteraryWorm, which consent LiteraryWorm may grant or refuse in its sole and absolute discretion.", "2. Reconstruct or attempt to discover any source code or algorithms of the Services, or any portion thereof, by any means whatsoever. Being able to see source code we publish doesn't give you a license to use it.", "3. Provide, or otherwise make available, the Services to any third party, other than the people in your household who use the profiles on your account.", "4. Intercept any data not intended for you.", "5. Damage, reveal, or alter any user's data, or any other hardware, software, or information relating to another person or entity."]}, {"heading": "AI Products", "paragraphs": ["When you use the AI Products provided by LiteraryWorm, you warrant that you will not:", "1. Try to make the AI Products produce content that this Policy forbids, or that breaks Anthropic's usage policies.", "2. Deploy AI techniques that utilize subliminal, manipulative, or deceptive methods designed to distort behavior and impair informed decision-making, particularly when such actions cause significant harm to individuals.", "3. Exploit vulnerabilities related to age, disability, or socio-economic circumstances through AI in a way that distorts behavior or decision-making, especially if this results in significant harm to the individual.", "4. Use AI systems for biometric categorization that infer sensitive attributes such as race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life, or sexual orientation, except in limited cases, such as labeling or filtering lawfully acquired datasets, or specific law enforcement activities.", "5. Implement AI-based social scoring systems that evaluate or classify individuals or groups based on their social behavior or personal traits in a manner that causes harm, discrimination, or unfair treatment.", "6. Assess the risk of an individual committing criminal offenses based solely on profiling, personality traits, or other non-behavioral factors, except in narrowly defined circumstances where legal safeguards are in place.", "7. Compile facial recognition databases through untargeted scraping of facial images from the internet, social media, or CCTV footage, unless it is part of a legally compliant and narrowly defined purpose.", "8. Use AI to infer emotions in sensitive environments such as workplaces, educational institutions, or any other context where such analysis could lead to discrimination, unfair treatment, or privacy violations.", "9. Engage in real-time remote biometric identification in public places for law enforcement purposes, except in specific situations where there are strong legal justifications and oversight mechanisms."]}, {"heading": "Artificial intelligence", "paragraphs": ["We recognize the significant impact AI can have on our users and society, and we are dedicated to ensuring that our AI Products are designed and operated in a manner that aligns with comprehensive ethical standards. We aim to use AI to enhance user experiences while upholding fairness, transparency, and accountability principles.", "That's why everything our AI Products write is labelled as written by AI, and why Ask the book and Who's who are only given the text up to your place in the book, and a quiz only the chapter it's about. A Previously… recap gets only the chapters before yours.", "This Policy applies to all AI-powered features, services, and systems in our Services. It governs the development, deployment, and use of AI technologies to protect users' rights and maintain transparency in all AI operations. This Policy applies to all stakeholders, including employees, third-party vendors, and partners who contribute to or interact with our AI Products.", "Enforcement. Any misuse of our AI Products or failure to adhere to the standards outlined in this Policy will result in appropriate actions to ensure the integrity of our platform and the protection of our users. The specific consequences for misuse of AI may vary depending on the nature and severity of the violation and the user's history with our Services.", "Violations may include, but are not limited to:", "1. Engaging the AI Products in ways that violate user privacy, manipulate data, disregard ethical guidelines, or are against AI service providers' terms of use (for our AI Products, Anthropic's).", "2. Deploying AI in a manner that introduces or causes bias, leading to unfair treatment of users or groups.", "3. Improper handling, storage, or use of data by AI Products, leading to breaches of user trust and legal compliance.", "4. Using AI in a way that compromises the privacy and security of our systems, data, or users.", "Depending on the violation, LiteraryWorm may take one or more of the following actions:", "Warnings: The responsible party may receive a formal warning and be required to cease violating practices.", "Temporary Suspension: In cases of repeated or more severe violations, the responsible individual's access to AI Products or certain features of our platform may be temporarily suspended while the issue is investigated.", "Termination of Access: Serious violations, particularly those that result in harm to users or breach privacy or other regulations, may lead to the permanent termination of access to our AI Products and Services.", "Legal Action: In cases where the misuse of AI leads to significant harm, data breaches, or legal violations, we may pursue legal action against the party responsible. This could include reporting the incident to law enforcement or regulatory bodies.", "Public Disclosure: For incidents that impact public trust or involve severe ethical breaches, we reserve the right to publicly disclose the violation and the actions taken in response to maintain transparency and accountability.", "Commitment to Responsible AI. In addition to the consequences outlined above, we are deeply committed to repairing any harm caused by the misuse of AI. This commitment is a testament to our dedication to our users and our responsibility as a company. We will correct biased outcomes and implement additional safeguards to prevent future violations.", "At LiteraryWorm, we are committed to the ongoing refinement and enhancement of our Policy. As technology evolves and regulatory environments shift, we recognize the importance of keeping our policies up to date to ensure that they remain relevant, effective, and aligned with best practices in AI ethics.", "We will regularly review and update our Policy to reflect technological advancements and legal changes in local, national, and international regulations related to AI. Our Policy will be updated as needed to comply with new laws and guidelines, ensuring that our practices remain legally sound and socially responsible."]}, {"heading": "Contributions", "paragraphs": ["In this Policy, the term \"Contributions\" means: any data, information, text, messages or other materials that you post, share, upload, submit, or otherwise provide in any manner on or through the Services, such as reading logs, ratings, book club posts, list names and descriptions, notes and highlights, and books you upload; or any other content, materials, or data you provide to LiteraryWorm or use with the Services.", "Some areas of the Services allow users to upload, transmit, or post Contributions. We may but are under no obligation to review or moderate the Contributions made on the Services, and we expressly exclude our liability for any loss or damage resulting from any of our users' breach of this Policy. Please report any Contribution that you believe breaches this Policy; however, we will determine, in our sole discretion, whether a Contribution is indeed in breach of this Policy.", "You warrant that:", "1. you are the creator and owner of or have the necessary licenses, rights, consents, releases, and permissions to use and to authorize us, the Services, and other users of the Services to use your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and this Policy;", "2. all your Contributions comply with applicable laws and are original and true (if they represent your opinion or facts);", "3. the creation, distribution, transmission, public display, or performance, and the accessing, downloading, or copying of your Contributions do not and will not infringe the proprietary rights, including but not limited to the copyright, patent, trademark, trade secret, or moral rights of any third party; and", "4. you have the verifiable consent, release, and/or permission of each and every identifiable individual person in your Contributions to use the name or likeness of each and every such identifiable individual person to enable inclusion and use of your Contributions in any manner contemplated by the Services and this Policy.", "You also agree that you will not post, transmit, or upload any (or any part of a) Contribution that:", "1. is in breach of applicable laws, regulation, court order, contractual obligation, this Policy, our Legal Terms, a legal duty, or that promotes or facilitates fraud or illegal activities;", "2. is defamatory, obscene, offensive, hateful, insulting, intimidating, bullying, abusive, or threatening, to any person or group;", "3. is false, inaccurate, or misleading;", "4. includes child sexual abuse material, or violates any applicable law intended to protect minors;", "5. contains any material that solicits personal information from anyone under the age of 18 or exploits people under the age of 18 in a sexual or violent manner;", "6. promotes violence, advocates the violent overthrow of any government, or incites, encourages, or threatens physical harm against another;", "7. is obscene, lewd, lascivious, filthy, violent, harassing, libelous, slanderous, contains sexually explicit material, or is otherwise objectionable (as determined by us);", "8. is discriminatory based on race, sex, religion, nationality, disability, sexual orientation, or age;", "9. bullies, intimidates, humiliates, or insults any person;", "10. promotes, facilitates, or assists anyone in promoting and facilitating acts of terrorism;", "11. infringes, or assists anyone in infringing, a third party's intellectual property rights or publicity or privacy rights;", "12. is deceitful, misrepresents your identity or affiliation with any person and/or misleads anyone as to your relationship with us or implies that the Contribution was made by someone else than you;", "13. contains unsolicited or unauthorized advertising, promotional materials, pyramid schemes, chain letters, spam, mass mailings, or other forms of solicitation that has been \"paid for,\" whether with monetary compensation or in kind; or", "14. misrepresents your identity or who the Contribution is from."]}, {"heading": "Reviews and ratings", "paragraphs": ["When your Contribution is a review or rating of a book, such as a rating or a reading log, you also agree that:", "1. you have firsthand experience with the book being reviewed;", "2. your Contribution is true to your experience;", "3. you are not affiliated with competitors if posting negative reviews (or linked in any way to, e.g., by being the author or publisher of, a book if posting positive reviews);", "4. you cannot make or offer any conclusions as to the legality of conduct;", "5. you cannot post any false or misleading statements; and", "6. you do not and will not organize a campaign encouraging others to post reviews, whether positive or negative."]}, {"heading": "Reporting a breach of this policy", "paragraphs": ["We may but are under no obligation to review or moderate the Contributions made on the Services and we expressly exclude our liability for any loss or damage resulting from any of our users' breach of this Policy.", "If you consider that any Service, Content, or Contribution breaches this Policy, please email us at report@literaryworm.com to let us know which Service, Content, or Contribution is in breach of this Policy and why.", "If you consider that any Service, Content, or Contribution infringes any third-party intellectual property rights, please email us at report@literaryworm.com. For a formal notice under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, follow the steps on our Copyright/DMCA page.", "You can also send detailed feedback on your interactions with our AI Products by emailing report@literaryworm.com. Please include specific details about the AI interaction, such as the book, the context, the nature of the concern, and any relevant screenshots or documentation.", "We will reasonably determine whether a Service, Content, or Contribution breaches this Policy."]}, {"heading": "Consequences of breaching this policy", "paragraphs": ["The consequences for violating our Policy will vary depending on the severity of the breach and the user's history on the Services, by way of example:", "We may, in some cases, give you a warning and/or remove the infringing Contribution, however, if your breach is serious or if you continue to breach our Legal Terms and this Policy, we have the right to suspend or terminate your access to and use of our Services and, if applicable, disable your account. We may also notify law enforcement or issue legal proceedings against you when we believe that there is a genuine risk to an individual or a threat to public safety.", "We exclude our liability for all action we may take in response to any of your breaches of this Policy."]}, {"heading": "Complaints and removal of legitimate content", "paragraphs": ["If you consider that some Content or Contribution has been mistakenly removed or blocked from the Services, please email us at report@literaryworm.com and we will promptly review our decision to remove such Content or Contribution. The Content or Contribution may stay \"down\" whilst we conduct the review process. If it was removed after a copyright notice, you can also send a counter-notice, as our Copyright/DMCA page explains."]}, {"heading": "Disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm is under no obligation to monitor users' activities, and we disclaim any responsibility for any user's misuse of the Services. LiteraryWorm has no responsibility for any user or other Content or Contribution created, maintained, stored, transmitted, or accessible on or through the Services, and is not obligated to monitor or exercise any editorial control over such material.", "If LiteraryWorm becomes aware that any such Content or Contribution violates this Policy, LiteraryWorm may, in addition to removing such Content or Contribution and blocking your account, report such breach to the police or appropriate regulatory authority.", "Unless otherwise stated in this Policy, LiteraryWorm disclaims any obligation to any person who has not entered into an agreement with LiteraryWorm for the use of the Services."]}, {"heading": "How can you contact us about this policy?", "paragraphs": ["If you have any further questions or comments or wish to report any problematic Content or Contribution, you may contact us by email: report@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["Memberships renew monthly or yearly until you cancel. Cancel at least 48 hours before your billing date to stop the next charge.", "Payments, including gift memberships, are final and aren't refunded, except where the law where you live says otherwise."]}, {"heading": "How billing works", "paragraphs": ["Your LiteraryWorm membership is billed through Stripe, monthly or yearly, until you cancel. Manage it in Account → Plan and billing, where you can also add or change your payment method.", "On monthly billing you can choose any billing day from the 1st to the 28th, and pause or cancel at any time. A yearly membership can be cancelled at any time, but not paused."]}, {"heading": "Cancelling", "paragraphs": ["Cancel at least 48 hours before your next billing date, and your plan stays active until the end of the period you've paid for, with no further charge.", "If you cancel less than 48 hours before your billing date, that charge still goes through and isn't refunded. A monthly plan then ends at the end of the month it pays for, and a yearly plan at the end of the year it pays for.", "Pausing a monthly membership stops billing until you resume. Your library, profiles and progress stay as they are."]}, {"heading": "Refunds", "paragraphs": ["All sales are final. No refunds are issued for memberships, renewals or time you didn't use.", "This doesn't affect any rights you have under the law where you live."]}, {"heading": "Gift memberships", "paragraphs": ["Gift memberships are paid once and are final too.", "A gift code doesn't expire, works once (from the day the gift starts, if the buyer chose a later day up to a year ahead; if the buyer asked us to email it to the person it's for, we send it once it can be redeemed, and otherwise we remind the buyer three days before a later start), and can't be exchanged for cash or refunded.", "Redeeming one gives its months free on the gift's plan; when they end, the membership ends unless a card has been added, and then it renews monthly until you cancel. Books that come with a gift are added to the library as Want to read when it's redeemed; they're LiteraryWorm titles, so reading and listening to them is part of the membership, not a separate purchase."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have any questions about this Return Policy, please contact us at support@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$How refunds work for LiteraryWorm memberships, and who to contact with questions.$lw$ then $lw$How billing, cancelling and refunds work for LiteraryWorm memberships and gift memberships, and who to contact with questions.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$returns$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Refunds", "paragraphs": ["This is not a demo app anymore: your LiteraryWorm account is a live account. You'll be billed monthly, or yearly if you choose, until you cancel. Add a payment method in Account → Plan and billing to continue your membership. On monthly billing you can change your billing day to any day from the 1st to the 28th, and start, pause or cancel billing at any time in Account; a yearly plan can be cancelled at any time, but not paused.", "All sales are final and no refund will be issued. You can cancel at any time from Account. Cancel at least 48 hours before your next billing date and your plan stays active until the end of the period you've paid for, and you won't be charged again. If you cancel less than 48 hours before your billing date, that charge still goes through (it isn't refunded) and your plan ends at the end of the month it pays for. You can also pause your membership, which stops billing until you resume.", "Gift memberships are paid once and are final too. A gift code doesn't expire, works once (from the day the gift starts, if the buyer chose a later day up to a year ahead; if the buyer asked us to email it to the person it's for, we send it once it can be redeemed, and otherwise we remind the buyer three days before a later start), and can't be exchanged for cash or refunded.", "Redeeming one gives its months free on the gift's plan; when they end, the membership ends unless a card has been added, and then it renews monthly until you cancel. Books that come with a gift are added to the library as Want to read when it's redeemed; they're LiteraryWorm titles, so reading and listening to them is part of the membership, not a separate purchase.", "This doesn't affect any rights you have under the law where you live."]}, {"heading": "Questions", "paragraphs": ["If you have any questions concerning our return policy, please contact us at support@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "In short", "paragraphs": ["The books you can read and hear in full here are in the public domain in the United States. Other titles show sample pages and details from Google Books.", "If you think something on LiteraryWorm infringes your copyright, send our designated agent a notice with the details listed below, and we'll act on it promptly."]}, {"heading": "Our books and their licences", "paragraphs": ["Public-domain titles use texts from Project Gutenberg and recordings from LibriVox, which LibriVox volunteers release into the public domain. These works are in the public domain in the United States, where LiteraryWorm operates. Our copies leave out Project Gutenberg's own header, footer and licence text.", "Other titles show sample pages written for LiteraryWorm, not the published books, and book details and covers come from Google Books under Google's terms.", "If you believe any of this is wrong, for example that a work isn't in the public domain, tell us using the steps below and we'll look into it promptly."]}, {"heading": "What people post or upload", "paragraphs": ["Reading logs, club posts and shared lists are written by members, who keep their rights in them. Books members upload are private to their own profile and aren't shown to anyone else (a book club started around one shows only its title and author); members must have the right to read them that way (see the Terms of Service).", "Audio clips members share are links to a short stretch of a public-domain LibriVox recording, played from the Internet Archive. Nothing is copied, cut or stored to make them."]}, {"heading": "Reporting content", "paragraphs": ["Users can report user-generated content and copyright infringement, and get information about the Acceptable Use Policy, by emailing report@literaryworm.com."]}, {"heading": "Reporting infringement", "paragraphs": ["If you believe something on LiteraryWorm infringes your copyright, send our designated agent a written notice that includes:", "your physical or electronic signature;", "the work you believe is infringed;", "the material on LiteraryWorm you want removed and where it is (a link helps);", "your name, address, phone number and email;", "a statement that you believe in good faith the use isn't authorised by the copyright owner, its agent or the law;", "and a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the notice is accurate and that you are, or are authorised to act for, the owner.", "Our designated agent's name, postal address, phone number and email, as registered with the U.S. Copyright Office, will be listed here before launch.", "We remove or disable access to the material, tell the member who posted it, and keep a record of the notice."]}, {"heading": "Counter-notices", "paragraphs": ["If your content was removed and you believe that was a mistake or that you had the right to post it, you may send a counter-notice with:", "your signature;", "what was removed and where it was;", "a statement, under penalty of perjury, that you believe in good faith it was removed by mistake or misidentification;", "your name, address and phone number;", "and your consent to the jurisdiction of the federal court for your address (or, outside the United States, any district where LiteraryWorm may be found) and to accept service from the person who sent the notice.", "We forward it to the person who sent the notice and may restore the content in 10 to 14 business days unless they tell us they've filed a court action."]}, {"heading": "Repeat infringers and false claims", "paragraphs": ["We close the accounts of members who repeatedly infringe copyright.", "Knowingly misrepresenting that material infringes, or that it was removed by mistake, can make you liable for damages under the DMCA, so please be sure before you send a notice or counter-notice."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$How LiteraryWorm respects copyright, which works are in the public domain, and how a rights holder can report content they believe infringes, under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA).$lw$ then $lw$How LiteraryWorm respects copyright, which works are in the public domain, and how a rights holder can report content they believe infringes, under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA).$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$copyright$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Our books and their licences", "paragraphs": ["Public-domain titles use texts from Project Gutenberg and recordings from LibriVox, which LibriVox volunteers release into the public domain. These works are in the public domain in the United States, where LiteraryWorm operates. Our copies leave out Project Gutenberg's own header, footer and licence text.", "Other titles show sample pages written for LiteraryWorm, not the published books, and book details and covers come from Google Books under Google's terms.", "If you believe any of this is wrong, for example that a work isn't in the public domain, tell us using the steps below and we'll look into it promptly."]}, {"heading": "What people post or upload", "paragraphs": ["Reading logs, club posts and shared lists are written by members, who keep their rights in them. Books members upload are private to their own profile and aren't shown to anyone else (a book club started around one shows only its title and author); members must have the right to read them that way (see the Terms of Service)."]}, {"heading": "Reporting content", "paragraphs": ["Users can report user-generated content and copyright infringement, and get information about the Acceptable Use Policy, by emailing report@literaryworm.com."]}, {"heading": "Reporting infringement", "paragraphs": ["If you believe something on LiteraryWorm infringes your copyright, send our designated agent a written notice that includes:", "your physical or electronic signature;", "the work you believe is infringed;", "the material on LiteraryWorm you want removed and where it is (a link helps);", "your name, address, phone number and email;", "a statement that you believe in good faith the use isn't authorised by the copyright owner, its agent or the law;", "and a statement, under penalty of perjury, that the notice is accurate and that you are, or are authorised to act for, the owner.", "Our designated agent's name, postal address, phone number and email, as registered with the U.S. Copyright Office, will be listed here before launch.", "We remove or disable access to the material, tell the member who posted it, and keep a record of the notice."]}, {"heading": "Counter-notices", "paragraphs": ["If your content was removed and you believe that was a mistake or that you had the right to post it, you may send a counter-notice with:", "your signature;", "what was removed and where it was;", "a statement, under penalty of perjury, that you believe in good faith it was removed by mistake or misidentification;", "your name, address and phone number;", "and your consent to the jurisdiction of the federal court for your address (or, outside the United States, any district where LiteraryWorm may be found) and to accept service from the person who sent the notice.", "We forward it to the person who sent the notice and may restore the content in 10 to 14 business days unless they tell us they've filed a court action."]}, {"heading": "Repeat infringers and false claims", "paragraphs": ["We close the accounts of members who repeatedly infringe copyright.", "Knowingly misrepresenting that material infringes, or that it was removed by mistake, can make you liable for damages under the DMCA, so please be sure before you send a notice or counter-notice."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Website disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["All information on the Site is provided in good faith, however we make no representation or warranty of any kind, express or implied, regarding the accuracy, adequacy, validity, reliability, availability, or completeness of any information on the Site. This includes book details and covers from Google Books, and everything written by AI, which is labelled as such (see below).", "UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCE SHALL WE HAVE ANY LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY LOSS OR DAMAGE OF ANY KIND INCURRED AS A RESULT OF THE USE OF THE SITE OR RELIANCE ON ANY INFORMATION PROVIDED ON THE SITE. YOUR USE OF THE SITE AND YOUR RELIANCE ON ANY INFORMATION ON THE SITE IS SOLELY AT YOUR OWN RISK."]}, {"heading": "AI-written content disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["Book summaries, content notes, Ask the book answers, translations, Who's who, Previously… recaps and chapter quizzes are written by AI (Claude, made by Anthropic) and labelled as written by AI.", "They can be wrong, leave things out, or miss what matters to you. Use them as a reading aid, not as a source of fact.", "Content notes in particular are a guide, not a guarantee. If a topic matters to you or a child at home, check the book itself before choosing it."]}, {"heading": "External links disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["The Site may contain (or you may be sent through the Site) links to other websites or content belonging to or originating from third parties, such as Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg. The Site doesn't show advertising. Such external links are not investigated, monitored, or checked for accuracy, adequacy, validity, reliability, availability, or completeness by us.", "WE DO NOT WARRANT, ENDORSE, GUARANTEE, OR ASSUME RESPONSIBILITY FOR THE ACCURACY OR RELIABILITY OF ANY INFORMATION OFFERED BY THIRD-PARTY WEBSITES LINKED THROUGH THE SITE. WE WILL NOT BE A PARTY TO OR IN ANY WAY BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MONITORING ANY TRANSACTION BETWEEN YOU AND THIRD-PARTY PROVIDERS OF PRODUCTS OR SERVICES."]}, {"heading": "Testimonials disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["The Site doesn't show testimonials at the moment. Reading logs and book club posts are written by members and belong to them; they don't reflect our views and opinions.", "If we add testimonials by users of our products and/or services, they will reflect the real-life experiences and opinions of such users. However, the experiences are personal to those particular users, and may not necessarily be representative of all users of our products and/or services. We do not claim, and you should not assume, that all users will have the same experiences. YOUR INDIVIDUAL RESULTS MAY VARY.", "Testimonials will be reviewed by us before being posted, and will appear on the Site verbatim as given by the users, except for the correction of grammar or typing errors. Some testimonials may be shortened for the sake of brevity where the full testimonial contained extraneous information not relevant to the general public.", "The views and opinions contained in testimonials belong solely to the individual user and do not reflect our views and opinions. Users will not be paid or otherwise compensated for their testimonials, and we'll say so if anyone who gives one is connected to us."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$The information provided by LiteraryWorm ("we," "us," or "our") on https://www.literaryworm.com (the "Site") is for general informational purposes only. This page explains what we can and can't promise about it, and about the other websites the Site links to.$lw$ then $lw$The information provided by LiteraryWorm ("we," "us," or "our") on https://www.literaryworm.com (the "Site") is for general informational purposes only. This page explains what we can and can't promise about it, and about the other websites the Site links to.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$disclaimer$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Website disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["All information on the Site is provided in good faith, however we make no representation or warranty of any kind, express or implied, regarding the accuracy, adequacy, validity, reliability, availability, or completeness of any information on the Site. This includes book details and covers from Google Books, and summaries, answers and quizzes written by AI, which are labelled as such.", "UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCE SHALL WE HAVE ANY LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ANY LOSS OR DAMAGE OF ANY KIND INCURRED AS A RESULT OF THE USE OF THE SITE OR RELIANCE ON ANY INFORMATION PROVIDED ON THE SITE. YOUR USE OF THE SITE AND YOUR RELIANCE ON ANY INFORMATION ON THE SITE IS SOLELY AT YOUR OWN RISK."]}, {"heading": "External links disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["The Site may contain (or you may be sent through the Site) links to other websites or content belonging to or originating from third parties, such as Google Books, the Internet Archive, LibriVox and Project Gutenberg. The Site doesn't show advertising. Such external links are not investigated, monitored, or checked for accuracy, adequacy, validity, reliability, availability, or completeness by us.", "WE DO NOT WARRANT, ENDORSE, GUARANTEE, OR ASSUME RESPONSIBILITY FOR THE ACCURACY OR RELIABILITY OF ANY INFORMATION OFFERED BY THIRD-PARTY WEBSITES LINKED THROUGH THE SITE. WE WILL NOT BE A PARTY TO OR IN ANY WAY BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MONITORING ANY TRANSACTION BETWEEN YOU AND THIRD-PARTY PROVIDERS OF PRODUCTS OR SERVICES."]}, {"heading": "Testimonials disclaimer", "paragraphs": ["The Site doesn't show testimonials at the moment. Reading logs and book club posts are written by members and belong to them; they don't reflect our views and opinions.", "If we add testimonials by users of our products and/or services, they will reflect the real-life experiences and opinions of such users. However, the experiences are personal to those particular users, and may not necessarily be representative of all users of our products and/or services. We do not claim, and you should not assume, that all users will have the same experiences. YOUR INDIVIDUAL RESULTS MAY VARY.", "Testimonials will be reviewed by us before being posted, and will appear on the Site verbatim as given by the users, except for the correction of grammar or typing errors. Some testimonials may be shortened for the sake of brevity where the full testimonial contained extraneous information not relevant to the general public.", "The views and opinions contained in testimonials belong solely to the individual user and do not reflect our views and opinions. Users will not be paid or otherwise compensated for their testimonials, and we'll say so if anyone who gives one is connected to us."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.legal_pages set sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Where do the books come from?", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm uses the Google Books API to show book details and covers when you browse and search, so you can find almost any book, save it to your library and write about it.", "Those covers, and the Google Books preview on some book pages, load from books.google.com, so Google sets its own third-party cookies on our website when they load. The Cookie Policy explains them, and blocking third-party cookies in your browser stops them without stopping LiteraryWorm.", "The books you can read and listen to in full are public-domain classics: texts from Project Gutenberg and recordings from LibriVox. Other LiteraryWorm titles show sample pages."]}, {"heading": "Can I read my own books?", "paragraphs": ["Yes. In My Library → Uploads, add EPUBs you own that have no DRM: up to 20 at a time, each up to 50 MB (a profile keeps up to 50). For example, buy a book that the publisher sells DRM-free on Google Play Books, download its EPUB from your Google Play Books library, then upload it to LiteraryWorm. Many publishers and stores sell DRM-free books, and public-domain EPUBs are free from Project Gutenberg and Standard Ebooks.", "Your upload opens in the reader with your place, bookmarks and highlights, and once you've opened it on a device, it keeps working there if your connection drops. Books with DRM can't be uploaded, and removing DRM to upload a book isn't allowed (see the Terms of Service)."]}, {"heading": "Reading and listening", "paragraphs": ["Open a book from its page with Read or Listen. Your place is shared between the two and across your devices. The mini-player keeps a book playing while you browse, and its controls also work from your lock screen and headphones.", "To read or listen without a connection, choose Read offline on a public-domain book's page. Each book's page has My journal for private, dated notes only you see; they're exported with your highlights from My Library → Notes. Words you keep from the dictionary come back for review in My words, after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while you know them. Your reading streak has two rest days a month, used automatically when you miss a day.", "In the reader, Display has OpenDyslexic among the fonts, and Reading guide: a reading ruler on one line, or line focus, which dims everything but three lines. It follows your pointer or a tap; J and K move it down or up a line.", "In the player (and the mini-player's More), Previously… catches you up on a public-domain book from the second chapter on: the story so far and the last chapter, written by AI from the chapters before yours only.", "On an audiobook's page, Read offline has Listen offline on a schedule: this device keeps the chapter you're on and the next 1, 3, 5 or 10 as you listen, on Wi-Fi only if you like, and can remove chapters you've finished. It counts as one of your plan's offline devices.", "In a public-domain book, select some words and choose Translate to read them in English, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese or Dutch. Only the words you selected are sent. Not on Kids profiles.", "In the player, or the mini-player's More menu, Share a clip makes a link to the last 15, 30 or 60 seconds you heard of a LibriVox recording. Anyone with the link can play that stretch."]}, {"heading": "Your library and reading tools", "paragraphs": ["A book's status can be Want to read, Reading, Finished or Didn't finish, for a book you put down; Didn't finish has its own tab in My Library, and recommendations stop suggesting books like it.", "To read a finished book again, choose Read again on its page. It goes back to Reading from the start, and finishing it again counts as another read, so the page says Your 2nd read or Read twice. Exports for Goodreads and StoryGraph carry the read count and dates.", "Under How did it feel? on a book's page, tag up to three moods, such as funny, hopeful, dark or tense, and a pace. My Library can show the books with one mood, Search lists the moods you've used, and Feel-good picks, a smart list and a row on Discover, gathers the cheerful ones.", "My Library → Smart lists fill themselves: Almost there (past halfway), Waiting for you (started, not opened for 30 days), From authors you follow and Loved it.", "A book's page shows Your time with this book once you've read or listened to it: time spent, the days, your pace through it and your biggest days.", "On a book's page, Reading plan lets you pick a day to finish by: it works out about how many minutes (at your own pace) or pages a day get you there, and says whether you're on track, ahead or behind; Home lists your plans.", "My Library → Notes has Review for highlights: each comes back the day after you make it, then after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while it still matters, up to 10 a day, and Home says when some are due.", "To take your library elsewhere, choose Export for Goodreads or Export for StoryGraph in My Library: you get a CSV of your books, shelves, star ratings (Love it 5, Like it 4, Not for me 2) and dates, made on your device, to import there."]}, {"heading": "Profiles, Kids and family", "paragraphs": ["Each person at home can have their own profile, with its own library and recommendations. Lock a profile with a PIN, set daily limits for younger readers, and change your plan, password or emails in Account. You can cancel or pause online at any time.", "A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "A grown-up can give a Kids profile a bedtime in its profile editor, with the account password: from 7pm to 10pm, and when reading starts again in the morning. Between them, on that device's clock, books and audiobooks show Time for bed and the place is saved; the password allows 15 more minutes.", "Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows.", "Each LiteraryWorm title's page has Content notes, written by AI: how much violence, death, frightening scenes, language, sexual content, alcohol and drugs, prejudice and self-harm it has, without spoilers. Grown-ups see them under a Kids profile's book requests too. They can miss things, so check anything that matters to you."]}, {"heading": "Book clubs and buddy reads", "paragraphs": ["On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on.", "Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like.", "A club can read a LiteraryWorm title or a book you uploaded, such as a DRM-free EPUB you bought. When you start a club in My Library → Clubs, choose LiteraryWorm books or My uploads under Book from, then find the book by title, author or ISBN (an ISBN is looked up on Google Books and matched by title and author). Sort the list by title, author, numbers first or series in reading order, and filter it to one series.", "Uploads stay private, so members don't get your file. The club shows the book's title and author, and each member uploads their own copy and chooses it on the club's page (Choose your copy). Posts, where everyone is and shared highlights then follow each member's place in their own copy, so nothing past their chapter is spoiled. An uploaded book has no recording, so there's no listening along.", "To read a book with one friend, choose Read with a friend on its page. A buddy read is a book club for two: send your friend its code, and you get spoiler-safe posts by chapter, meetings and shared highlights."]}, {"heading": "Your plan, notifications and gifts", "paragraphs": ["Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one.", "To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app.", "When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it."]}, {"heading": "Logging in and keeping your account safe", "paragraphs": ["In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use."]}, {"heading": "Trouble logging in?", "paragraphs": ["If Log in or Log in with a passkey does nothing, check that your browser isn't letting LiteraryWorm access your local network. LiteraryWorm never needs that permission, and allowing it can stop logging in from working. In Chrome and Edge, select the icon beside the address, choose Site settings, set Local network access to Block, then reload the page and log in again. If your browser asks whether LiteraryWorm can find devices on your local network, choose Block.", "Still stuck? Try a private or incognito window. If that works, a browser extension or something saved in your usual window is in the way. Otherwise, email support@literaryworm.com with your device and browser."]}, {"heading": "Report a problem", "paragraphs": ["Tell us what you were doing, the page you were on, and your device and browser, by email to support@literaryworm.com.", "For accessibility problems, email accessibility@literaryworm.com. To report a post, an upload or a copyright problem, email report@literaryworm.com. For privacy questions, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb,
  summary = case when summary = $lw$Answers to common questions about reading, listening, your library and your account, and how to report a problem.$lw$ then $lw$Answers to common questions about where the books come from, reading and listening, your library, your household, book clubs, your plan and logging in, and how to report a problem.$lw$ else summary end, updated_at = now()
where slug = $lw$help$lw$ and sections = $lw$[{"heading": "Where do the books come from?", "paragraphs": ["LiteraryWorm uses the Google Books API to show book details and covers when you browse and search, so you can find almost any book, save it to your library and write about it.", "Those covers, and the Google Books preview on some book pages, load from books.google.com, so Google sets its own third-party cookies on our website when they load. The Cookie Policy explains them, and blocking third-party cookies in your browser stops them without stopping LiteraryWorm.", "The books you can read and listen to in full are public-domain classics: texts from Project Gutenberg and recordings from LibriVox. Other LiteraryWorm titles show sample pages."]}, {"heading": "Can I read my own books?", "paragraphs": ["Yes. In My Library → Uploads, add EPUBs you own that have no DRM: up to 20 at a time, each up to 50 MB (a profile keeps up to 50). For example, buy a book that the publisher sells DRM-free on Google Play Books, download its EPUB from your Google Play Books library, then upload it to LiteraryWorm. Many publishers and stores sell DRM-free books, and public-domain EPUBs are free from Project Gutenberg and Standard Ebooks.", "Your upload opens in the reader with your place, bookmarks and highlights, and once you've opened it on a device, it keeps working there if your connection drops. Books with DRM can't be uploaded, and removing DRM to upload a book isn't allowed (see the Terms of Service)."]}, {"heading": "Reading and listening", "paragraphs": ["Open a book from its page with Read or Listen. Your place is shared between the two and across your devices. The mini-player keeps a book playing while you browse, and its controls also work from your lock screen and headphones.", "To read or listen without a connection, choose Read offline on a public-domain book's page. Each book's page has My journal for private, dated notes only you see; they're exported with your highlights from My Library → Notes. Words you keep from the dictionary come back for review in My words, after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while you know them. Your reading streak has two rest days a month, used automatically when you miss a day."]}, {"heading": "Your account and household", "paragraphs": ["Each person at home can have their own profile, with its own library and recommendations. Lock a profile with a PIN, set daily limits for younger readers, and change your plan, password or emails in Account. You can cancel or pause online at any time.", "In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use.", "A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "A grown-up can give a Kids profile a bedtime in its profile editor, with the account password: from 7pm to 10pm, and when reading starts again in the morning. Between them, on that device's clock, books and audiobooks show Time for bed and the place is saved; the password allows 15 more minutes.", "Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one.", "To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app.", "Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows.", "On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on.", "Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like.", "My Library → Smart lists fill themselves: Almost there (past halfway), Waiting for you (started, not opened for 30 days), From authors you follow and Loved it.", "A book's page shows Your time with this book once you've read or listened to it: time spent, the days, your pace through it and your biggest days.", "In the player (and the mini-player's More), Previously… catches you up on a public-domain book from the second chapter on: the story so far and the last chapter, written by AI from the chapters before yours only.", "My Library → Notes has Review for highlights: each comes back the day after you make it, then after 1, 3, 7, 14, 30 and 60 days while it still matters, up to 10 a day, and Home says when some are due.", "On a book's page, Reading plan lets you pick a day to finish by: it works out about how many minutes (at your own pace) or pages a day get you there, and says whether you're on track, ahead or behind; Home lists your plans.", "When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it.", "To take your library elsewhere, choose Export for Goodreads or Export for StoryGraph in My Library: you get a CSV of your books, shelves, star ratings (Love it 5, Like it 4, Not for me 2) and dates, made on your device, to import there.", "In the reader, Display has OpenDyslexic among the fonts, and Reading guide: a reading ruler on one line, or line focus, which dims everything but three lines. It follows your pointer or a tap; J and K move it down or up a line.", "On an audiobook's page, Read offline has Listen offline on a schedule: this device keeps the chapter you're on and the next 1, 3, 5 or 10 as you listen, on Wi-Fi only if you like, and can remove chapters you've finished. It counts as one of your plan's offline devices."]}, {"heading": "Your library, moods and more", "paragraphs": ["A book's status can be Want to read, Reading, Finished or Didn't finish, for a book you put down; Didn't finish has its own tab in My Library, and recommendations stop suggesting books like it.", "To read a finished book again, choose Read again on its page. It goes back to Reading from the start, and finishing it again counts as another read, so the page says Your 2nd read or Read twice. Exports for Goodreads and StoryGraph carry the read count and dates.", "Under How did it feel? on a book's page, tag up to three moods, such as funny, hopeful, dark or tense, and a pace. My Library can show the books with one mood, Search lists the moods you've used, and Feel-good picks, a smart list and a row on Discover, gathers the cheerful ones.", "Each LiteraryWorm title's page has Content notes, written by AI: how much violence, death, frightening scenes, language, sexual content, alcohol and drugs, prejudice and self-harm it has, without spoilers. Grown-ups see them under a Kids profile's book requests too. They can miss things, so check anything that matters to you.", "In a public-domain book, select some words and choose Translate to read them in English, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese or Dutch. Only the words you selected are sent. Not on Kids profiles.", "In the player, or the mini-player's More menu, Share a clip makes a link to the last 15, 30 or 60 seconds you heard of a LibriVox recording. Anyone with the link can play that stretch.", "To read a book with one friend, choose Read with a friend on its page. A buddy read is a book club for two: send your friend its code, and you get spoiler-safe posts by chapter, meetings and shared highlights."]}, {"heading": "Trouble logging in?", "paragraphs": ["If Log in or Log in with a passkey does nothing, check that your browser isn't letting LiteraryWorm access your local network. LiteraryWorm never needs that permission, and allowing it can stop logging in from working. In Chrome and Edge, select the icon beside the address, choose Site settings, set Local network access to Block, then reload the page and log in again. If your browser asks whether LiteraryWorm can find devices on your local network, choose Block.", "Still stuck? Try a private or incognito window. If that works, a browser extension or something saved in your usual window is in the way. Otherwise, email support@literaryworm.com with your device and browser."]}, {"heading": "Book clubs on your own books", "paragraphs": ["A club can read a LiteraryWorm title or a book you uploaded, such as a DRM-free EPUB you bought. When you start a club in My Library → Clubs, choose LiteraryWorm books or My uploads under Book from, then find the book by title, author or ISBN (an ISBN is looked up on Google Books and matched by title and author). Sort the list by title, author, numbers first or series in reading order, and filter it to one series.", "Uploads stay private, so members don't get your file. The club shows the book's title and author, and each member uploads their own copy and chooses it on the club's page (Choose your copy). Posts, where everyone is and shared highlights then follow each member's place in their own copy, so nothing past their chapter is spoiled. An uploaded book has no recording, so there's no listening along."]}, {"heading": "Report a problem", "paragraphs": ["Tell us what you were doing, the page you were on, and your device and browser, by email to support@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

insert into public.changelog_entries (released_on, version, kind, title, body, major)
select $lw$2026-11-01$lw$::date, $lw$2026.11$lw$, $lw$update$lw$, $lw$Clearer policies and Help$lw$, $lw$Your Privacy Choices, the Return Policy, the Terms of Service, the End User License Agreement, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Disclaimer, Copyright/DMCA, the Accessibility Policy and the Children's Privacy Notice are easier to read, most with an In short summary at the top, and up to date with content notes, Translate, audio clips and buddy reads. Help is grouped by topic: reading and listening, your library, profiles and family, book clubs, your plan, and logging in.$lw$, false
where not exists (select 1 from public.changelog_entries c where c.title = $lw$Clearer policies and Help$lw$ and c.version = $lw$2026.11$lw$);
